// Deterministic declarations, typed package interfaces, and local imports.
//
// This package is the first self-hosted semantic phase. It consumes one closed
// compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph and constructs the name set which later
// type and body work may read: a package scope shared by every source file, one
// child file scope per parsed Draft file, ordinary declarations in canonical
// file/source order, and import aliases bound to the exact canonical graph edge
// selected for that ImportClause. Target-condition materialization gives each
// package-level `when` and visible local scalar constant one stable product row,
// evaluates demanded values through explicit dependency edges, and appends
// exactly one branch to the same package scope without rebuilding an earlier
// symbol. A subsequent operation projects the resulting direct public
// declarations into source-ordered imported-name rows, giving `alias.member` a
// stable cross-package Symbol_Reference without copying spellings. The first
// typed continuation installs the predeclared scalar table, demands public
// declaration/value products, builds canonical scalar/structural/nominal
// interface type graphs, and reconstructs each dependency row into
// consumer-local Type_Ids.
// Its closed subset covers named scalar aliases/constants, pointers,
// multi-pointers, slices, fixed arrays, tuples, explicit globals, and fixed
// Draft procedure signatures, declaration-owned distinct types, and ordinary
// natural-layout structs. Other nominal aggregates, specialized struct layout,
// contracts, body checking, and general constant evaluation stay behind an
// explicit diagnostic rather than receiving provisional semantics.
//
// Semantic_Workspace owns only its contiguous tables. Symbol spellings, source
// ranges, syntax IDs, and graph-edge indices borrow the immutable Workspace_Graph,
// which must therefore outlive every lookup, dump, diagnostic render, and final
// destroy. Symbol and Scope IDs are stable u32 table indices until destroy.
// Package rows remain aligned with Workspace_Graph.packages, while file indices
// remain aligned with each nested Package.files table. Conditional regions,
// selections, and compile-time product values borrow syntax from those same
// files. Imported name spans are contiguous per Import_Binding and retain
// references into the target package's stable Symbol table. Interface type IDs
// are package-independent within one producer graph; imported typed rows own no
// allocation and contain only consumer Type_Ids plus graph/source-backed text.
//
// Collection follows the production C++ order exactly. All file scopes are
// allocated before any names; imports occupy only their file scope; declarations
// occupy the package scope; duplicate lookup is direct-scope linear lookup over
// the canonical declaration-order vector. This intentionally preserves the
// bootstrap's simple representation and diagnostic choice. If real package
// sizes later justify a deterministic secondary index, the vectors remain the
// semantic ordering authority.
//
// The current bootstrap gives an imported generic record instantiation
// different pointer identity when separate files in one package consume it.
// Keep the Dynamic-owning representation and all of its operations in this one
// module until that bootstrap limitation is repaired; splitting the package now
// would turn correct Scope/Semantic_Package pointers into type mismatches.
//
// Relevant specification: docs/specification/01-core-language.md sections 3-4
// and its expression rules for distinct identity, plus
// docs/specification/02-types-memory-runtime.md section 5. These cover
// file-local imports, package-wide declaration visibility, compile-time `when`
// contributing selected declarations without a scope, distinct types retaining
// underlying layout while remaining nominally unequal, and source-order natural
// aggregate field placement.
package compiler_sema

import core/array
import core/memory
import compiler/diagnostic as compiler_diagnostic
import compiler/source as compiler_source
import compiler/syntax as compiler_syntax
import compiler/text as compiler_text
import compiler/workspace as compiler_workspace

Invalid_Scope_Value :: ~cast[u32](0)
Invalid_Symbol_Value :: ~cast[u32](0)
Invalid_Compile_Time_Product_Value :: ~cast[u32](0)
Invalid_Type_Value :: ~cast[u32](0)
Invalid_Interface_Type_Value :: ~cast[u32](0)

// Scope_Id is an index into one Semantic_Package.scopes table. The all-ones
// value is the package scope's parent sentinel; IDs never cross package rows.
pub Scope_Id :: struct {
    value: u32,
}

// Symbol_Id is an index into one Semantic_Package.symbols table. The all-ones
// value represents a diagnosed duplicate which published no binding.
pub Symbol_Id :: struct {
    value: u32,
}

// Type_Id is an index into one Semantic_Package.types table. Type IDs are
// package-local even for builtins: a structural procedure reconstructed from
// an imported interface must use the consumer's IDs, never the producer's.
// The all-ones value is invalid. Rows are append-only and may move in storage;
// semantic data therefore retains IDs rather than pointers.
pub Type_Id :: struct {
    value: u32,
}

// Interface_Type_Id is local to one package's canonical interface type graph.
// It is never interchangeable with Type_Id. Import reconstructs each graph row
// into the consumer Type_Id domain before a qualified name becomes typed.
pub Interface_Type_Id :: struct {
    value: u32,
}

// Compile_Time_Product_Id is an index into one
// Semantic_Package.compile_time_products table. Product IDs never cross a
// package row. The all-ones value means that a waiting product currently has
// no prerequisite; it is not a table row or a diagnosed source failure.
Compile_Time_Product_Id :: struct {
    value: u32,
}

// Symbol_Reference is the first name identity which may cross a package
// boundary. package_id selects one Semantic_Workspace package row and symbol
// then indexes that row's stable symbol table. Equality is semantic only within
// the owning workspace result; the pair is not serialized across compiler runs.
pub Symbol_Reference :: struct {
    package_id: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
}

// scope_id_valid distinguishes a table row from the package-parent sentinel.
pub scope_id_valid :: proc(id: Scope_Id) -> bool {
    return id.value != Invalid_Scope_Value
}

// symbol_id_valid distinguishes a published binding from a failed declaration.
pub symbol_id_valid :: proc(id: Symbol_Id) -> bool {
    return id.value != Invalid_Symbol_Value
}

// type_id_valid distinguishes a package type row from an unfinished semantic
// product. Zero is a valid row containing the explicit invalid builtin.
pub type_id_valid :: proc(id: Type_Id) -> bool {
    return id.value != Invalid_Type_Value
}

interface_type_id_valid :: proc(id: Interface_Type_Id) -> bool {
    return id.value != Invalid_Interface_Type_Value
}

compile_time_product_id_valid :: proc(id: Compile_Time_Product_Id) -> bool {
    return id.value != Invalid_Compile_Time_Product_Value
}

invalid_scope_id :: proc() -> Scope_Id {
    return Scope_Id{value = Invalid_Scope_Value}
}

invalid_symbol_id :: proc() -> Symbol_Id {
    return Symbol_Id{value = Invalid_Symbol_Value}
}

invalid_type_id :: proc() -> Type_Id {
    return Type_Id{value = Invalid_Type_Value}
}

invalid_interface_type_id :: proc() -> Interface_Type_Id {
    return Interface_Type_Id{value = Invalid_Interface_Type_Value}
}

invalid_compile_time_product_id :: proc() -> Compile_Time_Product_Id {
    return Compile_Time_Product_Id{
        value = Invalid_Compile_Time_Product_Value,
    }
}

// Scope_Kind is intentionally limited to the scopes established at declaration
// collection. Procedure, type, block, and parametric scopes arrive with the
// semantic products which actually populate them.
pub Scope_Kind :: enum u8 {
    package_scope,
    file_scope,
}

// Symbol_Kind is primarily the declaration collector's best source-only
// classification. unresolved_declaration preserves the intentional ambiguity
// of `Name :: X` until X has been resolved as a type value or ordinary
// constant. field is reserved for named struct-member interface packets; the
// current collector does not insert fields into package/file scopes.
pub Symbol_Kind :: enum u8 {
    import_alias,
    unresolved_declaration,
    type,
    constant,
    variable,
    procedure,
    field,
}

// Visibility describes Draft package visibility only. Native linker export is
// an orthogonal Symbol_Flags property.
pub Visibility :: enum u8 {
    private,
    public,
}

// Syntax_Reference identifies one node inside one workspace package file. The
// file index must address a parsed Draft source row in the owning package.
pub Syntax_Reference :: struct {
    file_index: usize,
    node: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
}

// Symbol_Flags records source properties known without type resolution.
// parametric includes both an explicit parameter list and a procedure static
// pack; foreign/exported remain separate from Draft visibility.
pub Symbol_Flags :: struct {
    is_thread_local: bool,
    is_foreign: bool,
    exported: bool,
    parametric: bool,
}

// Symbol is one accepted direct binding. name_range and optional native ranges
// address syntax.source's immutable bytes; no spelling is copied. scope is the
// exact direct owner. linker_name_range retains the effective native spelling
// for a foreign/export declaration: the quoted `as` token when present, or the
// local binding name otherwise. foreign_provider_range retains the provider
// name which encloses a foreign declaration.
pub Symbol :: struct {
    kind: Symbol_Kind,
    visibility: Visibility,
    flags: Symbol_Flags,
    scope: Scope_Id,
    syntax: Syntax_Reference,
    name_range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
    has_foreign_provider: bool,
    foreign_provider_range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
    has_linker_name: bool,
    linker_name_range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
    // type becomes valid only after this declaration's typed product
    // completes. Source declaration collection never guesses an ambiguous
    // `Name :: expression` result.
    type: Type_Id,
}

// Scope owns direct Symbol_Ids in canonical declaration order. parent is
// invalid only for package. file_index is meaningful only for a file scope.
pub Scope :: struct {
    kind: Scope_Kind,
    parent: Scope_Id,
    file_index: usize,
    symbols: array.Dynamic[Symbol_Id],
}

// Semantic_File connects one parsed package file to its preallocated file scope.
// Assembly inputs contribute no row because they contain no Draft aliases.
pub Semantic_File :: struct {
    file_index: usize,
    scope: Scope_Id,
}

// Import_Binding connects one accepted file-local alias symbol to the exact
// source occurrence already resolved by Workspace_Graph. graph_import_index
// therefore provides both canonical target Package_Id and normalized path.
// imported_name_begin/count describe one contiguous span in the consumer's
// Semantic_Package.imported_names after bind_workspace_public_names succeeds;
// both are zero before that phase.
pub Import_Binding :: struct {
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
    graph_import_index: usize,
    imported_name_begin: usize,
    imported_name_count: usize,
    typed_name_begin: usize,
    typed_name_count: usize,
}

// Imported_Name is one file-local alias member. declaration points directly to
// the target package's public source symbol; its spelling and source range are
// therefore borrowed through the graph and target Semantic_Package rather than
// copied into the consumer. Rows are ordered by import occurrence, then target
// package declaration order.
pub Imported_Name :: struct {
    import_symbol: Symbol_Id,
    declaration: Symbol_Reference,
}

// Semantic_Type_Kind is the first self-hosted subset of the specification's
// canonical type vocabulary. The order follows production TypeKind so
// later rows can be added without changing the identity of an existing kind.
// The distinct name is required because Draft already predeclares Type_Kind as
// the public reflection result enum; reusing it would bind annotations to that
// language type instead of this staging representation.
// This slice constructs every predeclared scalar plus the pointer, multi-pointer,
// slice, fixed-array, tuple, and procedure structural families plus named
// distinct declarations and ordinary natural-layout structs. Enums, variants,
// unions, SIMD, specialized struct layout, and parametric constructors remain a
// diagnosed staging boundary even though their final enum cases are reserved.
pub Semantic_Type_Kind :: enum u8 {
    invalid_type,
    void_type,
    untyped_integer_type,
    untyped_float_type,
    boolean_type,
    boolean_storage_type,
    signed_integer_type,
    unsigned_integer_type,
    float_type,
    rune_type,
    endian_scalar_type,
    raw_pointer_type,
    c_string_type,
    string_type,
    pointer_type,
    multi_pointer_type,
    slice_type,
    array_type,
    tuple_type,
    procedure_type,
    simd_vector_type,
    struct_type,
    enumeration_type,
    variant_type,
    union_type,
    distinct_named_type,
    type_parameter_type,
    meta_type_value,
}

// Semantic_Type is one package-local type identity. layout_known, byte_size,
// and byte_alignment contain the target-natural value layout; alignment is a
// positive power of two even when layout is unavailable. Scalar rows use name
// and bit_width; endian, pointer, multi-pointer, slice, array, and distinct rows
// additionally use element. Array rows use the positive element_count as part
// of identity. A distinct or struct row uses the three nominal byte views as
// its exact semantic key; name remains empty because qualified diagnostic
// display can be synthesized without allocating a redundant joined spelling.
// Tuple rows use one contiguous source-order span in
// Semantic_Package.type_members; procedure rows use the same representation
// with fixed parameter types followed by the result type. name points only at
// a process literal in this slice. Nominal views borrow either the owning
// Workspace_Package identity/source name or a dependency interface row; the
// workspace graph outlives every semantic package, so the row owns no
// allocation. nominal_member_begin/count address Semantic_Package.nominal_members
// only for completed structs; structural member_begin/count continue to address
// the ordered Type_Id span used by tuples, procedures, and struct member types.
pub Semantic_Type :: struct {
    kind: Semantic_Type_Kind,
    name: string,
    nominal_root_identity: []u8,
    nominal_root_relative_path: []u8,
    nominal_public_name: []u8,
    layout_known: bool,
    byte_size: u64,
    byte_alignment: u32,
    bit_width: u32,
    element: Type_Id,
    element_count: u64,
    member_begin: usize,
    member_count: usize,
    nominal_member_begin: usize,
    nominal_member_count: usize,
}

// Semantic_Nominal_Member is one source-order field in a completed local or
// reconstructed struct. name borrows source/interface storage, type belongs to
// the containing package's Type_Id domain, and byte_offset is the natural Draft
// offset. The current closed slice admits only Symbol_Kind.field and natural
// field placement; retaining kind makes the interface packet explicit without
// pretending enum or variant members are already implemented.
Semantic_Nominal_Member :: struct {
    name: []u8,
    kind: Symbol_Kind,
    type: Type_Id,
    byte_offset: u64,
}

// Compile_Time_Value_Kind is the closed value domain currently publishable by
// the self-hosted constant products. The five target categories remain
// distinct until the general enum representation arrives. type_value names an
// exact Type_Id and therefore never crosses a package interface directly.
Compile_Time_Value_Kind :: enum u8 {
    invalid,
    boolean,
    unsigned_integer,
    string_value,
    architecture,
    operating_system,
    abi,
    byte_order,
    object_format,
    type_value,
}

// Compile_Time_Value owns no allocation. static_type and type_value use the
// owning Semantic_Package's Type_Id domain. Text is either a process-lifetime
// target/builtin spelling or a source-backed view selected by text_from_source;
// the workspace graph outlives every value and imported copy.
Compile_Time_Value :: struct {
    kind: Compile_Time_Value_Kind,
    static_type: Type_Id,
    boolean: bool,
    unsigned_integer: u64,
    profile_text: string,
    source_text: []u8,
    text_from_source: bool,
    type_value: Type_Id,
}

// Interface_Type is a package-independent graph row. element and the member
// span refer only to the same package's interface type table; element_count is
// the positive fixed-array length and otherwise zero. Distinct and struct rows
// carry the defining package's content identity, package-relative path, and
// original declaration name. Those byte views are persistent semantic
// identity: an importing package copies them unchanged when it re-exports the
// type. Layout fields and nominal_member_begin/count carry the complete
// natural-layout struct packet without producer-local IDs. Rows are
// appended lazily in public declaration discovery order, matching production's
// InterfaceBuilder and installing a placeholder before following children so
// later recursive nominal graphs have an honest seam.
pub Interface_Type :: struct {
    kind: Semantic_Type_Kind,
    name: string,
    nominal_root_identity: []u8,
    nominal_root_relative_path: []u8,
    nominal_public_name: []u8,
    layout_known: bool,
    byte_size: u64,
    byte_alignment: u32,
    bit_width: u32,
    element: Interface_Type_Id,
    element_count: u64,
    member_begin: usize,
    member_count: usize,
    nominal_member_begin: usize,
    nominal_member_count: usize,
}

// Interface_Nominal_Member is Semantic_Nominal_Member after its Type_Id has
// been translated into the producer's interface graph. Names and offsets are
// package-independent semantic facts; the row owns no allocation.
Interface_Nominal_Member :: struct {
    name: []u8,
    kind: Symbol_Kind,
    type: Interface_Type_Id,
    byte_offset: u64,
}

// Interface_Constant_Value is Compile_Time_Value after every Type_Id has been
// rewritten into the package-independent interface graph. Text remains a
// borrowed immutable spelling; no source coordinate or physical path enters
// interface identity.
Interface_Constant_Value :: struct {
    kind: Compile_Time_Value_Kind,
    static_type: Interface_Type_Id,
    boolean: bool,
    unsigned_integer: u64,
    profile_text: string,
    source_text: []u8,
    text_from_source: bool,
    type_value: Interface_Type_Id,
}

// Interface_Declaration is one public package binding in final selected source
// order. source_symbol is retained only for this process-level migration oracle;
// persistent interface identity is the declaration name plus its canonical
// type/value graph. type is always valid on a completed interface row.
pub Interface_Declaration :: struct {
    source_symbol: Symbol_Id,
    name: []u8,
    kind: Symbol_Kind,
    flags: Symbol_Flags,
    type: Interface_Type_Id,
    has_constant: bool,
    constant: Interface_Constant_Value,
}

// Imported_Type memoizes one dependency Interface_Type_Id reconstruction in a
// consumer package. target_package plus interface_type is the lookup key;
// local_type belongs exclusively to the consumer. Struct import installs this
// row immediately after creating its nominal shell, before following recursive
// members. A second path to the same nominal type may have another memo row but
// converges through the nominal interner. Rows are command-local and never
// serialized or used for output ordering.
Imported_Type :: struct {
    target_package: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    interface_type: Interface_Type_Id,
    local_type: Type_Id,
}

// Imported_Typed_Name is the typed continuation of Imported_Name. declaration
// retains producer source identity, interface_ordinal selects the exact public
// interface row, kind preserves type declarations without manufacturing a
// constant, and local_type/constant have already been reconstructed into the
// consumer Type_Id domain. Rows follow import occurrence then producer public
// declaration order.
pub Imported_Typed_Name :: struct {
    import_symbol: Symbol_Id,
    declaration: Symbol_Reference,
    interface_ordinal: usize,
    name: []u8,
    kind: Symbol_Kind,
    local_type: Type_Id,
    has_constant: bool,
    constant: Compile_Time_Value,
}

// Conditional_Declaration is one unmaterialized package-level `when`. syntax
// names the parsed WhenDeclaration, scope is the surrounding package scope, and
// collection_context preserves foreign/export facts which apply if the chosen
// branch is appended. materialized changes exactly once after a selection is
// published. The row borrows all source and owns no allocation.
Conditional_Declaration :: struct {
    syntax: Syntax_Reference,
    scope: Scope_Id,
    collection_context: Collection_Context,
    materialized: bool,
}

// Conditional_Selection is the immutable boolean result for one recorded
// declaration condition. Rows follow materialization order; an `else when`
// appears only after the false predecessor exposes it.
pub Conditional_Selection :: struct {
    syntax: Syntax_Reference,
    select_true: bool,
}

// Compile_Time_Product_Kind distinguishes a named scalar constant value from a
// package branch decision or declaration type. Conditions use condition_index;
// declarations and constants use symbol. Declaration rows remain dormant until
// interface construction demands a public binding or one of its dependencies.
Compile_Time_Product_Kind :: enum u8 {
    condition,
    declaration,
    constant,
}

// Compile_Time_Use selects the staging diagnostic at the one shared constant
// evaluator boundary. It is an enum rather than a boolean because the caller
// is choosing a semantic consumer, not toggling an implementation detail.
Compile_Time_Use :: enum u8 {
    target_selection,
    typed_interface,
}

// Compile_Time_Product_State is monotonic. dormant constant rows preserve the
// production source-order index without evaluating unrelated constants.
// waiting rows are demanded and may name one exact unpublished prerequisite;
// complete rows own one immutable scalar value, declaration classification, or
// selected branch; error is terminal. A blocked attempt records only its first
// missing value, then is retried after that product completes. The single
// dependency field is the complete ready-edge set for the current attempt
// rather than hidden recursion.
Compile_Time_Product_State :: enum u8 {
    dormant,
    waiting,
    complete,
    error,
}

// Compile_Time_Product is one stable row in Semantic_Package's append-only
// compile-time table. Conditions are appended in discovered site order before
// currently visible constant candidates; selected branches extend that same
// order. dependency names another row in this table and never a Symbol_Id from
// another package. value is meaningful for a completed constant and may be
// retained by its declaration product; declaration type identity lives on the
// Symbol. The row owns no allocation and may move when its Dynamic table grows.
Compile_Time_Product :: struct {
    kind: Compile_Time_Product_Kind,
    state: Compile_Time_Product_State,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
    condition_index: usize,
    dependency: Compile_Time_Product_Id,
    value: Compile_Time_Value,
}

// Semantic_Package owns every collected row for one aligned workspace package.
// graph_import_edges is a private source-order index built in one workspace-wide
// graph scan; it avoids repeated global edge scans while aliases are collected.
pub Semantic_Package :: struct {
    workspace_package: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    package_scope: Scope_Id,
    scopes: array.Dynamic[Scope],
    symbols: array.Dynamic[Symbol],
    files: array.Dynamic[Semantic_File],
    imports: array.Dynamic[Import_Binding],
    imported_names: array.Dynamic[Imported_Name],
    types: array.Dynamic[Semantic_Type],
    type_members: array.Dynamic[Type_Id],
    nominal_members: array.Dynamic[Semantic_Nominal_Member],
    imported_types: array.Dynamic[Imported_Type],
    imported_typed_names: array.Dynamic[Imported_Typed_Name],
    interface_types: array.Dynamic[Interface_Type],
    interface_type_members: array.Dynamic[Interface_Type_Id],
    interface_nominal_members: array.Dynamic[Interface_Nominal_Member],
    interface_type_translations: array.Dynamic[Interface_Type_Id],
    interface_declarations: array.Dynamic[Interface_Declaration],
    conditional_declarations: array.Dynamic[Conditional_Declaration],
    conditional_selections: array.Dynamic[Conditional_Selection],
    compile_time_products: array.Dynamic[Compile_Time_Product],
    indexed_condition_count: usize,
    indexed_compile_time_symbol_count: usize,
    unconditional_symbol_count: usize,
    graph_import_edges: array.Dynamic[usize],
    typed_interface_built: bool,
}

Diagnostic_Code :: enum u8 {
    duplicate_declaration,
    previous_declaration,
    thread_local_non_variable,
    parametric_non_type_or_procedure,
    linker_name_non_native,
    grouped_type,
    grouped_procedure,
    unsupported_target_condition,
    unsupported_typed_interface,
    cyclic_typed_interface,
}

// Semantic_Diagnostic is one source-backed row in deterministic collection
// order. Dynamic messages are assembled only while rendering, so the semantic
// graph owns no duplicated identifier strings.
Semantic_Diagnostic :: struct {
    severity: compiler_diagnostic.Severity,
    code: Diagnostic_Code,
    package_id: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    file_index: usize,
    range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
    scope_kind: Scope_Kind,
}

// Semantic_Workspace owns package rows aligned to the canonical input graph and
// a single cross-package diagnostic sequence. failed is true exactly when an
// error (not a note) was appended. target_declarations_materialized changes
// once after every supported package condition has selected a branch;
// public_names_bound changes after the chosen declaration table is complete and
// the imported-name spans are ready.
pub Semantic_Workspace :: struct {
    packages: array.Dynamic[Semantic_Package],
    diagnostics: array.Dynamic[Semantic_Diagnostic],
    failed: bool,
    target_declarations_materialized: bool,
    public_names_bound: bool,
    typed_interfaces_built: bool,
}

Collection_Context :: struct {
    flags: Symbol_Flags,
    has_foreign_provider: bool,
    foreign_provider_range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
}

Collector :: struct {
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    workspace_package: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Package,
    graph_import_cursor: usize,
}

bytes_equal :: proc(left, right: []u8) -> bool {
    if len(left) != len(right) {
        return false
    }
    for index: usize = 0; index < len(left); index += 1 {
        if left[index] != right[index] {
            return false
        }
    }
    return true
}

bytes_equal_text :: proc(bytes: []u8, text: string) -> bool {
    if len(bytes) != len(text) {
        return false
    }
    for index: usize = 0; index < len(bytes); index += 1 {
        if bytes[index] != text[index] {
            return false
        }
    }
    return true
}

token_is_contextual_name :: proc(kind: compiler_syntax.Token_Kind) -> bool {
    switch kind {
    case .identifier, .keyword_c, .keyword_type, .keyword_integer,
        .keyword_float, .keyword_number, .keyword_flags, .keyword_memory,
        .keyword_bits:
        return true
    case:
        return false
    }
}

scope_kind_text :: proc(kind: Scope_Kind) -> string {
    switch kind {
    case .package_scope: return "package"
    case .file_scope: return "file"
    }
    return "unknown"
}

// symbol_kind_text is the stable migration-dump spelling shared with the C++
// oracle. It is not a source keyword table.
pub symbol_kind_text :: proc(kind: Symbol_Kind) -> string {
    switch kind {
    case .import_alias: return "import"
    case .unresolved_declaration: return "unresolved-declaration"
    case .type: return "type"
    case .constant: return "constant"
    case .variable: return "variable"
    case .procedure: return "procedure"
    case .field: return "field"
    }
    return "unknown"
}

visibility_text :: proc(visibility: Visibility) -> string {
    switch visibility {
    case .private: return "private"
    case .public: return "public"
    }
    return "unknown"
}

source_file :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    package_id: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    file_index: usize,
) -> ^compiler_source.Source_File {
    assert(compiler_workspace.package_id_valid(package_id),
        "semantic source package ID is invalid")
    assert(cast[usize](package_id.value) < graph.packages.length,
        "semantic source package ID exceeds graph")
    loaded := &graph.packages.data[cast[usize](package_id.value)].loaded
    assert(file_index < compiler_workspace.file_count(loaded),
        "semantic source file index exceeds package")
    source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(loaded, file_index)
    assert(source_row.parsed,
        "semantic source reference names an unparsed file")
    return &source_row.source
}

source_bytes :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    package_id: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    file_index: usize,
    range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
) -> []u8 {
    return compiler_source.bytes_in_range(
        source_file(graph, package_id, file_index),
        range,
    )
}

symbol_name_bytes :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    symbol: ^Symbol,
) -> []u8 {
    return source_bytes(
        graph,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        symbol.syntax.file_index,
        symbol.name_range,
    )
}

append_diagnostic :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    severity: compiler_diagnostic.Severity,
    code: Diagnostic_Code,
    package_id: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    file_index: usize,
    range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
    scope_kind: Scope_Kind,
) {
    array.append(&semantic.diagnostics, Semantic_Diagnostic{
        severity = severity,
        code = code,
        package_id = package_id,
        file_index = file_index,
        range = range,
        scope_kind = scope_kind,
    })
    if severity == .error {
        semantic.failed = true
    }
}

add_scope :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    kind: Scope_Kind,
    parent: Scope_Id,
    file_index: usize,
) -> Scope_Id {
    assert(semantic_package.scopes.length < cast[usize](Invalid_Scope_Value),
        "semantic scope table exceeds u32 identity space")
    if scope_id_valid(parent) {
        assert(cast[usize](parent.value) < semantic_package.scopes.length,
            "semantic scope parent is not yet published")
    } else {
        assert(kind == .package_scope,
            "only a package scope may have no parent")
    }

    id := Scope_Id{value = cast[u32](semantic_package.scopes.length)}
    scope: Scope
    scope.kind = kind
    scope.parent = parent
    scope.file_index = file_index
    array.init(&scope.symbols)
    array.append(&semantic_package.scopes, scope)
    empty: Scope
    scope = empty
    return id
}

// lookup_direct performs exact byte lookup only in scope. The returned symbol
// is the first canonical declaration and therefore the duplicate diagnostic's
// stable previous binding.
pub lookup_direct :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    scope: Scope_Id,
    name: []u8,
) -> (Symbol_Id, bool) {
    assert(scope_id_valid(scope), "semantic direct lookup scope is invalid")
    assert(cast[usize](scope.value) < semantic_package.scopes.length,
        "semantic direct lookup scope exceeds table")
    owner := &semantic_package.scopes.data[cast[usize](scope.value)]
    for index: usize = 0; index < owner.symbols.length; index += 1 {
        id := owner.symbols.data[index]
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[cast[usize](id.value)]
        if bytes_equal(
            symbol_name_bytes(graph, semantic_package, symbol),
            name,
        ) {
            return (id, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_symbol_id(), false)
}

// lookup walks direct scopes from file to package. It makes an import alias an
// ordinary file-local shadow while keeping declarations visible to every file.
pub lookup :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    scope: Scope_Id,
    name: []u8,
) -> (Symbol_Id, bool) {
    current := scope
    for scope_id_valid(current) {
        (found, exists) := lookup_direct(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            current,
            name,
        )
        if exists {
            return (found, true)
        }
        current = semantic_package.scopes.data[
            cast[usize](current.value)
        ].parent
    }
    return (invalid_symbol_id(), false)
}

declare_symbol :: proc(
    collector: ^Collector,
    symbol: Symbol,
) -> Symbol_Id {
    name := source_bytes(
        collector.graph,
        collector.semantic_package.workspace_package,
        symbol.syntax.file_index,
        symbol.name_range,
    )
    (previous, duplicate) := lookup_direct(
        collector.graph,
        collector.semantic_package,
        symbol.scope,
        name,
    )
    if duplicate {
        owner := &collector.semantic_package.scopes.data[
            cast[usize](symbol.scope.value)
        ]
        append_diagnostic(
            collector.semantic,
            .error,
            .duplicate_declaration,
            collector.semantic_package.workspace_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            symbol.name_range,
            owner.kind,
        )
        previous_symbol := &collector.semantic_package.symbols.data[
            cast[usize](previous.value)
        ]
        append_diagnostic(
            collector.semantic,
            .note,
            .previous_declaration,
            collector.semantic_package.workspace_package,
            previous_symbol.syntax.file_index,
            previous_symbol.name_range,
            owner.kind,
        )
        return invalid_symbol_id()
    }

    assert(collector.semantic_package.symbols.length <
        cast[usize](Invalid_Symbol_Value),
        "semantic symbol table exceeds u32 identity space")
    id := Symbol_Id{
        value = cast[u32](collector.semantic_package.symbols.length),
    }
    owner_scope := symbol.scope
    array.append(&collector.semantic_package.symbols, symbol)
    array.append(
        &collector.semantic_package.scopes.data[
            cast[usize](owner_scope.value)
        ].symbols,
        id,
    )
    return id
}

node_has_token_before :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    node: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Node,
    end: u32,
    wanted: compiler_syntax.Token_Kind,
) -> bool {
    bounded_end := end
    if bounded_end > node.token_end {
        bounded_end = node.token_end
    }
    for index := node.token_begin; index < bounded_end; index += 1 {
        if tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)].kind == wanted {
            return true
        }
    }
    return false
}

declaration_payload :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    declaration_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> (compiler_syntax.Node_Id, bool) {
    declaration := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, declaration_id)
    if declaration.child_count < 2 {
        return (compiler_syntax.Node_Id{}, false)
    }
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, declaration_id)
    candidate := children[len(children) - 1]
    kind := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, candidate).kind
    if kind == .binding_pattern || kind == .tuple_pattern ||
        kind == .parametric_parameter_list {
        return (compiler_syntax.Node_Id{}, false)
    }
    return (candidate, true)
}

node_is_type_syntax :: proc(kind: compiler_syntax.Node_Kind) -> bool {
    switch kind {
    case .named_type, .pointer_type, .multi_pointer_type, .slice_type,
        .array_type, .simd_type, .tuple_type, .procedure_type,
        .distinct_type, .struct_type, .enum_type, .variant_type, .union_type:
        return true
    case:
        return false
    }
}

declaration_kind :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    declaration: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Node,
    collection_context: Collection_Context,
    payload: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    has_payload: bool,
) -> Symbol_Kind {
    header_end := declaration.token_end
    if has_payload {
        header_end = compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, payload).token_begin
    }
    immutable := node_has_token_before(
        tree,
        declaration,
        header_end,
        .colon_colon,
    )
    if !immutable {
        return .variable
    }
    if !has_payload {
        return .unresolved_declaration
    }

    payload_kind := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, payload).kind
    if payload_kind == .procedure {
        return .procedure
    }
    if payload_kind == .procedure_type &&
        collection_context.flags.is_foreign {
        return .procedure
    }
    if node_is_type_syntax(payload_kind) {
        return .type
    }
    if payload_kind == .name_expression ||
        payload_kind == .member_expression ||
        payload_kind == .bracket_expression ||
        payload_kind == .group_expression ||
        payload_kind == .tuple_expression {
        return .unresolved_declaration
    }
    return .constant
}

linker_name_range :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    declaration_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> (compiler_source.Source_Range, bool) {
    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, declaration_id) {
        child := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id)
        if child.kind != .link_name_clause {
            continue
        }
        for index := child.token_begin; index < child.token_end; index += 1 {
            token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)]
            if token.kind == .string_literal {
                return (token.range, true)
            }
        }
    }
    return (compiler_source.Source_Range{}, false)
}

procedure_has_static_pack :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    payload: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    has_payload: bool,
) -> bool {
    if !has_payload {
        return false
    }
    procedure := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, payload)
    if procedure.kind != .procedure && procedure.kind != .procedure_type {
        return false
    }
    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, payload) {
        child := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id)
        if child.kind != .parameter_list {
            continue
        }
        for parameter_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, child_id) {
            for part_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
                tree,
                parameter_id,
            ) {
                if compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, part_id).kind ==
                    .static_pack_type {
                    return true
                }
            }
        }
    }
    return false
}

pattern_name_count :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    pattern_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> usize {
    count: usize = 0
    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, pattern_id) {
        child := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id)
        if child.kind != .name_list {
            continue
        }
        for index := child.token_begin; index < child.token_end; index += 1 {
            if token_is_contextual_name(
                tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)].kind,
            ) {
                count += 1
            }
        }
    }
    return count
}

report_declaration_error :: proc(
    collector: ^Collector,
    code: Diagnostic_Code,
    syntax: Syntax_Reference,
    range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
) {
    append_diagnostic(
        collector.semantic,
        .error,
        code,
        collector.semantic_package.workspace_package,
        syntax.file_index,
        range,
        .package_scope,
    )
}

collect_declaration :: proc(
    collector: ^Collector,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    file_index: usize,
    declaration_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    scope: Scope_Id,
    collection_context: Collection_Context,
) {
    declaration := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, declaration_id)
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, declaration_id)
    if len(children) == 0 {
        return
    }
    pattern_id := children[0]
    pattern := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, pattern_id)
    if pattern.kind != .binding_pattern && pattern.kind != .tuple_pattern {
        return
    }

    (payload, has_payload) := declaration_payload(tree, declaration_id)
    kind := declaration_kind(
        tree,
        declaration,
        collection_context,
        payload,
        has_payload,
    )
    flags := collection_context.flags
    for child_id in children {
        if compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id).kind ==
            .parametric_parameter_list {
            flags.parametric = true
        }
    }
    if procedure_has_static_pack(tree, payload, has_payload) {
        flags.parametric = true
    }
    flags.is_thread_local = node_has_token_before(
        tree,
        declaration,
        pattern.token_begin,
        .keyword_thread_local,
    )
    visibility: Visibility = .private
    if node_has_token_before(
        tree,
        declaration,
        pattern.token_begin,
        .keyword_pub,
    ) {
        visibility = .public
    }
    (link_range, has_link_name) := linker_name_range(tree, declaration_id)
    syntax := Syntax_Reference{file_index = file_index, node = declaration_id}

    if flags.is_thread_local && kind != .variable {
        report_declaration_error(
            collector,
            .thread_local_non_variable,
            syntax,
            declaration.range,
        )
    }
    if flags.parametric && kind != .type && kind != .procedure &&
        kind != .unresolved_declaration {
        report_declaration_error(
            collector,
            .parametric_non_type_or_procedure,
            syntax,
            declaration.range,
        )
    }
    if has_link_name && !flags.is_foreign && !flags.exported {
        report_declaration_error(
            collector,
            .linker_name_non_native,
            syntax,
            link_range,
        )
    }

    name_count := pattern_name_count(tree, pattern_id)
    if kind == .type && name_count > 1 {
        report_declaration_error(
            collector,
            .grouped_type,
            syntax,
            pattern.range,
        )
    } else if kind == .procedure && name_count > 1 {
        report_declaration_error(
            collector,
            .grouped_procedure,
            syntax,
            pattern.range,
        )
    }

    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, pattern_id) {
        child := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id)
        if child.kind != .name_list {
            continue
        }
        for index := child.token_begin; index < child.token_end; index += 1 {
            token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)]
            if !token_is_contextual_name(token.kind) {
                continue
            }
            name := compiler_source.bytes_in_range(
                source_file(
                    collector.graph,
                    collector.semantic_package.workspace_package,
                    file_index,
                ),
                token.range,
            )
            if bytes_equal_text(name, "_") {
                continue
            }

            symbol: Symbol
            symbol.kind = kind
            symbol.visibility = visibility
            symbol.flags = flags
            symbol.scope = scope
            symbol.syntax = syntax
            symbol.name_range = token.range
            symbol.has_foreign_provider =
                collection_context.has_foreign_provider
            symbol.foreign_provider_range =
                collection_context.foreign_provider_range
            symbol.type = invalid_type_id()
            if flags.is_foreign || flags.exported {
                symbol.has_linker_name = true
                symbol.linker_name_range = token.range
                if has_link_name {
                    symbol.linker_name_range = link_range
                }
            }
            declare_symbol(collector, symbol)
        }
    }
}

foreign_provider_range :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    foreign_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> (compiler_source.Source_Range, bool) {
    foreign_node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, foreign_id)
    for index := foreign_node.token_begin + 1;
        index < foreign_node.token_end;
        index += 1 {
        token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)]
        if token_is_contextual_name(token.kind) {
            return (token.range, true)
        }
    }
    return (compiler_source.Source_Range{}, false)
}

collect_item :: proc(
    collector: ^Collector,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    file_index: usize,
    node_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    scope: Scope_Id,
    collection_context: Collection_Context,
) {
    node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, node_id)
    switch node.kind {
    case .declaration:
        collect_declaration(
            collector,
            tree,
            file_index,
            node_id,
            scope,
            collection_context,
        )
    case .foreign_block:
        nested := collection_context
        nested.flags.is_foreign = true
        (provider, has_provider) := foreign_provider_range(tree, node_id)
        nested.foreign_provider_range = provider
        nested.has_foreign_provider = has_provider
        children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, node_id)
        if len(children) != 0 {
            collect_declaration_list(
                collector,
                tree,
                file_index,
                children[len(children) - 1],
                scope,
                nested,
            )
        }
    case .export_declaration:
        nested := collection_context
        nested.flags.exported = true
        children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, node_id)
        if len(children) != 0 {
            collect_item(
                collector,
                tree,
                file_index,
                children[0],
                scope,
                nested,
            )
        }
    case .deny_declaration:
        children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, node_id)
        if len(children) != 0 {
            collect_declaration_list(
                collector,
                tree,
                file_index,
                children[len(children) - 1],
                scope,
                collection_context,
            )
        }
    case .declaration_list:
        collect_declaration_list(
            collector,
            tree,
            file_index,
            node_id,
            scope,
            collection_context,
        )
    case .when_declaration:
        array.append(
            &collector.semantic_package.conditional_declarations,
            Conditional_Declaration{
                syntax = Syntax_Reference{
                    file_index = file_index,
                    node = node_id,
                },
                scope = scope,
                collection_context = collection_context,
            },
        )
    case:
        // Docs, judgments, and synthesis do not publish an ordinary name
        // during this phase.
    }
}

collect_declaration_list :: proc(
    collector: ^Collector,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    file_index: usize,
    list_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    scope: Scope_Id,
    collection_context: Collection_Context,
) {
    list := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, list_id)
    if list.kind != .declaration_list {
        return
    }
    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, list_id) {
        collect_item(
            collector,
            tree,
            file_index,
            child_id,
            scope,
            collection_context,
        )
    }
}

collect_import :: proc(
    collector: ^Collector,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    file_index: usize,
    import_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    file_scope: Scope_Id,
) {
    import_node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, import_id)
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, import_id)
    if len(children) == 0 {
        return
    }
    path := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[0])

    alias_range: compiler_source.Source_Range
    have_alias := false
    for index := path.token_begin; index < path.token_end; index += 1 {
        token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)]
        if token_is_contextual_name(token.kind) {
            alias_range = token.range
            have_alias = true
        }
    }
    if !have_alias {
        return
    }
    for index := path.token_end; index < import_node.token_end; index += 1 {
        if tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)].kind != .keyword_as {
            continue
        }
        if index + 1 < import_node.token_end {
            alias := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index + 1)]
            if token_is_contextual_name(alias.kind) {
                alias_range = alias.range
            }
        }
        break
    }

    // A successful closed Workspace_Graph has exactly one edge for every
    // parsed import clause. Per-package edge lists preserve source order even
    // though recursive dependency edges may appear between global rows.
    assert(collector.graph_import_cursor <
        collector.semantic_package.graph_import_edges.length,
        "semantic import has no canonical workspace edge")
    graph_import_index := collector.semantic_package.graph_import_edges.data[
        collector.graph_import_cursor
    ]
    collector.graph_import_cursor += 1
    graph_import := &collector.graph.imports.data[graph_import_index]
    assert(graph_import.file_index == file_index &&
        graph_import.syntax.value == import_id.value,
        "semantic import order differs from canonical workspace edges")

    symbol: Symbol
    symbol.kind = .import_alias
    symbol.visibility = .private
    symbol.scope = file_scope
    symbol.syntax = Syntax_Reference{
        file_index = file_index,
        node = import_id,
    }
    symbol.name_range = alias_range
    id := declare_symbol(collector, symbol)
    if symbol_id_valid(id) {
        array.append(&collector.semantic_package.imports, Import_Binding{
            symbol = id,
            graph_import_index = graph_import_index,
        })
    }
}

collect_file :: proc(
    collector: ^Collector,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    file_scope: Scope_Id,
) {
    if !compiler_syntax.node_id_valid(tree.root) {
        return
    }
    collection_context: Collection_Context
    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, tree.root) {
        child := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id)
        if child.kind == .import_clause {
            collect_import(
                collector,
                tree,
                file_index,
                child_id,
                file_scope,
            )
        } else if child.kind == .declaration_list {
            collect_declaration_list(
                collector,
                tree,
                file_index,
                child_id,
                collector.semantic_package.package_scope,
                collection_context,
            )
        }
    }
}

collect_package :: proc(collector: ^Collector) {
    collector.semantic_package.package_scope = add_scope(
        collector.semantic_package,
        .package_scope,
        invalid_scope_id(),
        0,
    )

    // Allocate every file scope before names so scope IDs and the scope graph
    // do not depend on an earlier semantic error.
    loaded := &collector.workspace_package.loaded
    for file_index: usize = 0;
        file_index < compiler_workspace.file_count(loaded);
        file_index += 1 {
        source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(loaded, file_index)
        if !source_row.parsed ||
            !compiler_syntax.node_id_valid(source_row.tree.root) {
            continue
        }
        scope := add_scope(
            collector.semantic_package,
            .file_scope,
            collector.semantic_package.package_scope,
            file_index,
        )
        array.append(&collector.semantic_package.files, Semantic_File{
            file_index = file_index,
            scope = scope,
        })
    }

    for index: usize = 0;
        index < collector.semantic_package.files.length;
        index += 1 {
        semantic_file := collector.semantic_package.files.data[index]
        source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(
            loaded,
            semantic_file.file_index,
        )
        collect_file(
            collector,
            semantic_file.file_index,
            &source_row.tree,
            semantic_file.scope,
        )
    }
    assert(collector.graph_import_cursor ==
        collector.semantic_package.graph_import_edges.length,
        "canonical workspace edge has no semantic import clause")
    collector.semantic_package.unconditional_symbol_count =
        collector.semantic_package.symbols.length
}

// append_semantic_type assigns the next stable package-local Type_Id. The
// caller supplies a complete plain row and retains no pointer across growth.
append_semantic_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    semantic_type: Semantic_Type,
) -> Type_Id {
    assert(semantic_package.types.length < cast[usize](Invalid_Type_Value),
        "semantic type table exceeds u32 identity space")
    id := Type_Id{value = cast[u32](semantic_package.types.length)}
    array.append(&semantic_package.types, semantic_type)
    return id
}

// append_builtin_type installs one predeclared scalar or scalar-like row. Its
// element is invalid unless the caller later fills an endian/compiler-enum
// relationship. Builtin names are process literals and require no cleanup.
append_builtin_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    kind: Semantic_Type_Kind,
    name: string,
    bit_width: u32 = 0,
) -> Type_Id {
    layout_known := bit_width != 0
    byte_size := cast[u64](bit_width / 8)
    byte_alignment := bit_width / 8
    if byte_alignment == 0 {
        byte_alignment = 1
    }
    return append_semantic_type(
        semantic_package,
        Semantic_Type{
            kind = kind,
            name = name,
            layout_known = layout_known,
            byte_size = byte_size,
            byte_alignment = byte_alignment,
            bit_width = bit_width,
            element = invalid_type_id(),
        },
    )
}

// append_endian_type records the native scalar behind one byte-order-specific
// storage identity. The spelling is still retained for deterministic dumps and
// direct predeclared lookup.
append_endian_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    name: string,
    native: Type_Id,
    bit_width: u32,
) {
    native_type := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](native.value)]
    append_semantic_type(
        semantic_package,
        Semantic_Type{
            kind = .endian_scalar_type,
            name = name,
            layout_known = native_type.layout_known,
            byte_size = native_type.byte_size,
            byte_alignment = native_type.byte_alignment,
            bit_width = bit_width,
            element = native,
        },
    )
}

// init_semantic_types reproduces the production TypeStore's fixed builtin
// order. Process-local numeric equality is not persistent identity, but keeping
// the same order makes debugging and later differential expansion direct. All
// four current targets use 64-bit natural/pointer integers.
init_semantic_types :: proc(semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package) {
    array.init(&semantic_package.types)
    array.init(&semantic_package.type_members)
    array.init(&semantic_package.nominal_members)
    array.init(&semantic_package.imported_types)
    array.init(&semantic_package.imported_typed_names)
    array.init(&semantic_package.interface_types)
    array.init(&semantic_package.interface_type_members)
    array.init(&semantic_package.interface_nominal_members)
    array.init(&semantic_package.interface_type_translations)
    array.init(&semantic_package.interface_declarations)

    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .invalid_type, "<invalid>")
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .void_type,
        name = "<void>",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        element = invalid_type_id(),
    })
    append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .untyped_integer_type,
        "<untyped integer>",
    )
    append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .untyped_float_type,
        "<untyped float>",
    )
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .boolean_type, "bool", 8)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .boolean_storage_type, "b8", 8)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .boolean_storage_type, "b16", 16)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .boolean_storage_type, "b32", 32)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .boolean_storage_type, "b64", 64)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .signed_integer_type, "i8", 8)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .signed_integer_type, "i16", 16)
    i32_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .signed_integer_type,
        "i32",
        32,
    )
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .signed_integer_type, "i64", 64)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .signed_integer_type, "i128", 128)
    u8_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "u8",
        8,
    )
    u16_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "u16",
        16,
    )
    u32_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "u32",
        32,
    )
    u64_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "u64",
        64,
    )
    u128_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "u128",
        128,
    )
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .signed_integer_type, "int", 64)
    uint_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "uint",
        64,
    )
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .signed_integer_type, "isize", 64)
    usize_type := append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "usize",
        64,
    )
    append_builtin_type(
        semantic_package,
        .unsigned_integer_type,
        "uintptr",
        64,
    )
    f16_type := append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .float_type, "f16", 16)
    f32_type := append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .float_type, "f32", 32)
    f64_type := append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .float_type, "f64", 64)
    append_semantic_type(
        semantic_package,
        Semantic_Type{
            kind = .rune_type,
            name = "rune",
            layout_known = true,
            byte_size = 4,
            byte_alignment = 4,
            bit_width = 32,
            element = i32_type,
        },
    )

    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i16le", Type_Id{value = 10}, 16)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i16be", Type_Id{value = 10}, 16)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i32le", i32_type, 32)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i32be", i32_type, 32)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i64le", Type_Id{value = 12}, 64)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i64be", Type_Id{value = 12}, 64)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i128le", Type_Id{value = 13}, 128)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "i128be", Type_Id{value = 13}, 128)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u16le", u16_type, 16)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u16be", u16_type, 16)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u32le", u32_type, 32)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u32be", u32_type, 32)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u64le", u64_type, 64)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u64be", u64_type, 64)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u128le", u128_type, 128)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "u128be", u128_type, 128)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "f16le", f16_type, 16)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "f16be", f16_type, 16)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "f32le", f32_type, 32)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "f32be", f32_type, 32)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "f64le", f64_type, 64)
    append_endian_type(semantic_package, "f64be", f64_type, 64)

    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .raw_pointer_type, "rawptr", 64)
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .c_string_type, "cstring", 64)
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .string_type,
        name = "string",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 16,
        byte_alignment = 8,
        element = invalid_type_id(),
    })
    append_builtin_type(semantic_package, .meta_type_value, "type")
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Type_Kind",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Type_Byte_Order",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Calling_Convention",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Target_Architecture",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Target_Operating_System",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Target_ABI",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Target_Byte_Order",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .enumeration_type,
        name = "Target_Object_Format",
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 1,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        bit_width = 8,
        element = u8_type,
    })
    assert(semantic_package.types.length == 62,
        "self-hosted builtin type order diverged from production")
    assert(uint_type.value == 20 && usize_type.value == 22,
        "natural integer builtin IDs diverged from production")
}


// Natural_Layout is the target-independent result shared by structural tuple
// construction and ordinary struct completion. known is false only while one
// member still lacks layout; overflow is reported separately by the caller so
// an impossible size cannot be confused with a schedulable dependency.
Natural_Layout :: struct {
    known: bool,
    overflow: bool,
    size: u64,
    alignment: u32,
}

// aligned_offset rounds one byte position to a positive member alignment.
// Layout arithmetic is source-controlled, so overflow returns false rather
// than wrapping and manufacturing a smaller aggregate.
aligned_offset :: proc(value: u64, alignment: u32) -> (u64, bool) {
    assert(alignment != 0, "type layout has zero alignment")
    divisor := cast[u64](alignment)
    remainder := value % divisor
    if remainder == 0 {
        return (value, true)
    }
    increment := divisor - remainder
    if value > ~cast[u64](0) - increment {
        return (0, false)
    }
    return (value + increment, true)
}

// compute_natural_layout applies Draft's source-order aggregate algorithm to
// an already resolved list of member types. It deliberately does not retain
// offsets: tuples need only the aggregate layout, while struct completion uses
// the companion operation below to publish offsets with its named fields.
compute_natural_layout :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    members: []Type_Id,
) -> Natural_Layout {
    result := Natural_Layout{alignment = 1}
    for member_id in members {
        assert(type_id_valid(member_id) &&
            cast[usize](member_id.value) < semantic_package.types.length,
            "natural layout received an invalid member type")
        member := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](member_id.value)]
        if !member.layout_known {
            return result
        }
        (offset, aligned) := aligned_offset(
            result.size,
            member.byte_alignment,
        )
        if !aligned || member.byte_size > ~cast[u64](0) - offset {
            result.overflow = true
            return result
        }
        result.size = offset + member.byte_size
        if member.byte_alignment > result.alignment {
            result.alignment = member.byte_alignment
        }
    }
    (final_size, aligned) := aligned_offset(result.size, result.alignment)
    if !aligned {
        result.overflow = true
        return result
    }
    result.known = true
    result.size = final_size
    return result
}

// find_builtin_type performs exact predeclared lookup. byte is a true alias of
// u8 and therefore returns the existing row rather than creating a second type.
find_builtin_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    name: []u8,
) -> (Type_Id, bool) {
    if bytes_equal_text(name, "byte") {
        return (Type_Id{value = 14}, true)
    }
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.types.length; index += 1 {
        candidate := &semantic_package.types.data[index]
        if strings_equal(candidate.name, "<invalid>") ||
            strings_equal(candidate.name, "<void>") ||
            strings_equal(candidate.name, "<untyped integer>") ||
            strings_equal(candidate.name, "<untyped float>") {
            continue
        }
        if bytes_equal_text(name, candidate.name) {
            return (Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_type_id(), false)
}

// intern_element_type returns the canonical identity for one pointer-like
// structural constructor. Only the three element-only kinds admitted by this
// phase are valid callers; keeping that invariant here prevents an enum value
// from silently constructing an incomplete array, SIMD, or nominal row. The
// direct scan preserves append order as the semantic ordering authority.
intern_element_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    kind: Semantic_Type_Kind,
    element: Type_Id,
) -> Type_Id {
    assert(kind == .pointer_type || kind == .multi_pointer_type ||
        kind == .slice_type,
        "element-only type interner received an unsupported kind")
    assert(type_id_valid(element),
        "element-only type interner received an invalid element")
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.types.length; index += 1 {
        candidate := &semantic_package.types.data[index]
        if candidate.kind == kind && candidate.element.value == element.value {
            return Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}
        }
    }
    layout_size: u64 = 8
    layout_alignment: u32 = 8
    if kind == .slice_type {
        layout_size = 16
    }
    return append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = kind,
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = layout_size,
        byte_alignment = layout_alignment,
        element = element,
    })
}

// intern_array_type returns the canonical fixed-array identity. count is
// already a checked positive compile-time usize value; zero is source failure,
// never an incomplete row. Element and count together form structural identity.
intern_array_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    element: Type_Id,
    count: u64,
) -> Type_Id {
    assert(type_id_valid(element),
        "array type interner received an invalid element")
    assert(count != 0, "array type interner received a zero element count")
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.types.length; index += 1 {
        candidate := &semantic_package.types.data[index]
        if candidate.kind == .array_type &&
            candidate.element.value == element.value &&
            candidate.element_count == count {
            element_type := &semantic_package.types.data[
                cast[usize](element.value)
            ]
            candidate.layout_known = element_type.layout_known
            candidate.byte_alignment = element_type.byte_alignment
            candidate.byte_size = 0
            if candidate.layout_known {
                if element_type.byte_size != 0 &&
                    count > ~cast[u64](0) / element_type.byte_size {
                    candidate.layout_known = false
                } else {
                    candidate.byte_size = element_type.byte_size * count
                }
            }
            return Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}
        }
    }
    element_type := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](element.value)]
    layout_known := element_type.layout_known
    byte_size: u64 = 0
    if layout_known {
        if element_type.byte_size != 0 &&
            count > ~cast[u64](0) / element_type.byte_size {
            layout_known = false
        } else {
            byte_size = element_type.byte_size * count
        }
    }
    return append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .array_type,
        layout_known = layout_known,
        byte_size = byte_size,
        byte_alignment = element_type.byte_alignment,
        element = element,
        element_count = count,
    })
}

// intern_tuple_type returns the canonical ordered product identity. A Draft 1
// tuple has at least two members; the parser has already distinguished grouped
// syntax, but this layer retains the semantic invariant. The member span is
// appended only after the direct scan proves no equal tuple already exists.
intern_tuple_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    members: []Type_Id,
) -> Type_Id {
    assert(len(members) >= 2, "tuple type has fewer than two members")
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.types.length; index += 1 {
        candidate := &semantic_package.types.data[index]
        if candidate.kind != .tuple_type ||
            candidate.member_count != len(members) {
            continue
        }
        equal := true
        for member_index: usize = 0;
            member_index < len(members);
            member_index += 1 {
            if semantic_package.type_members.data[
                    candidate.member_begin + member_index
                ].value != members[member_index].value {
                equal = false
                break
            }
        }
        if equal {
            layout := compute_natural_layout(semantic_package, members)
            candidate.layout_known = layout.known
            candidate.byte_size = layout.size
            candidate.byte_alignment = layout.alignment
            return Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}
        }
    }
    begin := semantic_package.type_members.length
    for member in members {
        assert(type_id_valid(member),
            "tuple type interner received an invalid member")
        array.append(&semantic_package.type_members, member)
    }
    layout := compute_natural_layout(semantic_package, members)
    return append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .tuple_type,
        layout_known = layout.known,
        byte_size = layout.size,
        byte_alignment = layout.alignment,
        element = invalid_type_id(),
        member_begin = begin,
        member_count = len(members),
    })
}

// intern_procedure_type returns the canonical structural identity for fixed
// parameter types followed by one result type. The direct scan is deliberate:
// interface fixtures are small, ordering stays inspectable, and a measured
// deterministic index can later replace only this lookup mechanism.
intern_procedure_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    members: []Type_Id,
) -> Type_Id {
    assert(len(members) != 0, "procedure type has no result member")
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.types.length; index += 1 {
        candidate := &semantic_package.types.data[index]
        if candidate.kind != .procedure_type ||
            candidate.member_count != len(members) {
            continue
        }
        equal := true
        for member_index: usize = 0;
            member_index < len(members);
            member_index += 1 {
            if semantic_package.type_members.data[
                    candidate.member_begin + member_index
                ].value != members[member_index].value {
                equal = false
                break
            }
        }
        if equal {
            return Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}
        }
    }
    begin := semantic_package.type_members.length
    for member in members {
        array.append(&semantic_package.type_members, member)
    }
    return append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .procedure_type,
        layout_known = true,
        byte_size = 8,
        byte_alignment = 8,
        element = invalid_type_id(),
        member_begin = begin,
        member_count = len(members),
    })
}

// intern_distinct_type returns the one package-local row for a declaration's
// persistent nominal identity. Unlike structural interning, equality is not
// based on the underlying type: two declarations over u32 remain different.
// Reconstructing the same foreign distinct through two import paths does reuse
// the row, because root content identity, package-relative path, and original
// declaration name together denote one Draft type. A repeated key with a
// different underlying Type_Id is an inconsistent interface graph and is
// rejected by returning invalid rather than silently changing type meaning.
intern_distinct_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    root_identity, root_relative_path, public_name: []u8,
    underlying: Type_Id,
) -> Type_Id {
    assert(len(root_identity) != 0 && len(root_relative_path) != 0 &&
        len(public_name) != 0,
        "distinct type has an incomplete nominal identity")
    assert(type_id_valid(underlying),
        "distinct type has an invalid underlying type")
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.types.length; index += 1 {
        candidate := &semantic_package.types.data[index]
        if candidate.kind != .distinct_named_type ||
            !bytes_equal(candidate.nominal_root_identity, root_identity) ||
            !bytes_equal(
                candidate.nominal_root_relative_path,
                root_relative_path,
            ) ||
            !bytes_equal(candidate.nominal_public_name, public_name) {
            continue
        }
        if candidate.element.value != underlying.value {
            return invalid_type_id()
        }
        source := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](underlying.value)]
        candidate.layout_known = source.layout_known
        candidate.byte_size = source.byte_size
        candidate.byte_alignment = source.byte_alignment
        return Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}
    }
    source := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](underlying.value)]
    return append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .distinct_named_type,
        nominal_root_identity = root_identity,
        nominal_root_relative_path = root_relative_path,
        nominal_public_name = public_name,
        layout_known = source.layout_known,
        byte_size = source.byte_size,
        byte_alignment = source.byte_alignment,
        element = underlying,
    })
}

// intern_struct_type_shell returns the one package-local identity for a named
// struct before its fields or natural layout are necessarily complete. The
// shell is the semantic recursion seam: pointer fields may refer to it, while a
// by-value use observes layout_known == false and becomes an explicit product
// dependency rather than recursing through syntax.
intern_struct_type_shell :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    root_identity, root_relative_path, public_name: []u8,
) -> Type_Id {
    assert(len(root_identity) != 0 && len(root_relative_path) != 0 &&
        len(public_name) != 0,
        "struct type has an incomplete nominal identity")
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.types.length; index += 1 {
        candidate := &semantic_package.types.data[index]
        if candidate.kind == .struct_type &&
            bytes_equal(candidate.nominal_root_identity, root_identity) &&
            bytes_equal(
                candidate.nominal_root_relative_path,
                root_relative_path,
            ) &&
            bytes_equal(candidate.nominal_public_name, public_name) {
            return Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}
        }
    }
    return append_semantic_type(semantic_package, Semantic_Type{
        kind = .struct_type,
        nominal_root_identity = root_identity,
        nominal_root_relative_path = root_relative_path,
        nominal_public_name = public_name,
        byte_alignment = 1,
        element = invalid_type_id(),
    })
}

// missing_layout_symbol traces a structural type whose layout is not yet known
// to the local nominal declaration that owns its completion product. Pointer,
// slice, and procedure values stop before their pointee/signature because their
// own layout is already known. The currently admitted by-value constructors are
// acyclic until they reach an incomplete struct shell; direct and mutual
// by-value struct cycles therefore produce ordinary product edges.
missing_layout_symbol :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    type_id: Type_Id,
) -> (Symbol_Id, bool) {
    if !type_id_valid(type_id) ||
        cast[usize](type_id.value) >= semantic_package.types.length {
        return (invalid_symbol_id(), false)
    }
    semantic_type := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](type_id.value)]
    if semantic_type.layout_known {
        return (invalid_symbol_id(), false)
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .struct_type {
        for index: usize = 0;
            index < semantic_package.symbols.length;
            index += 1 {
            if semantic_package.symbols.data[index].type.value == type_id.value {
                return (Symbol_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}, true)
            }
        }
        return (invalid_symbol_id(), false)
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .array_type ||
        semantic_type.kind == .distinct_named_type {
        return missing_layout_symbol(semantic_package, semantic_type.element)
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .tuple_type {
        for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_type.member_count; index += 1 {
            (dependency, found) := missing_layout_symbol(
                semantic_package,
                semantic_package.type_members.data[
                    semantic_type.member_begin + index
                ],
            )
            if found {
                return (dependency, true)
            }
        }
    }
    return (invalid_symbol_id(), false)
}

// complete_plain_struct_type resolves exactly the ordinary Draft 1 struct
// subset and publishes its type-member span, named-field span, offsets, and
// natural layout together. A field node must have one unmodified type child;
// C representation, explicit aggregate alignment, packed/bit fields, selected
// member regions, synthesized members, and member directives remain at the
// diagnosed staging boundary. Temporary rows prevent a blocked attempt from
// leaking a partial member packet into the stable package tables.
complete_plain_struct_type :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    struct_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    struct_type: Type_Id,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    blocked_symbol: ^Symbol_Id,
) -> bool {
    struct_row := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](struct_type.value)]
    if struct_row.layout_known {
        return true
    }
    node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, struct_id)
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, struct_id)
    if node.kind != .struct_type || len(children) != 1 {
        return false
    }
    member_list := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[0])
    if member_list.kind != .member_list {
        return false
    }

    field_types: array.Dynamic[Type_Id]
    fields: array.Dynamic[Semantic_Nominal_Member]
    array.init(&field_types)
    array.init(&fields)
    valid := true
    for field_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, children[0]) {
        field := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, field_id)
        field_children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, field_id)
        if field.kind != .field_member || len(field_children) != 1 ||
            !node_is_type_syntax(
                compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(
                    tree,
                    field_children[0],
                ).kind,
            ) {
            valid = false
            break
        }
        (field_type, resolved) := resolve_type_syntax(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            field_children[0],
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
        )
        if !resolved {
            valid = false
            break
        }
        type_node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, field_children[0])
        name_count: usize = 0
        for token_index := field.token_begin;
            token_index < type_node.token_begin;
            token_index += 1 {
            token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](token_index)]
            if !token_is_contextual_name(token.kind) {
                continue
            }
            name := source_bytes(
                graph,
                semantic_package.workspace_package,
                file_index,
                token.range,
            )
            if bytes_equal_text(name, "_") {
                valid = false
                break
            }
            duplicate := false
            for existing in array.view(&fields) {
                if bytes_equal(existing.name, name) {
                    duplicate = true
                    break
                }
            }
            if duplicate {
                valid = false
                break
            }
            array.append(&field_types, field_type)
            array.append(&fields, Semantic_Nominal_Member{
                name = name,
                kind = .field,
                type = field_type,
            })
            name_count += 1
        }
        if !valid || name_count == 0 {
            valid = false
            break
        }
    }
    if !valid || fields.length == 0 {
        array.destroy(&fields)
        array.destroy(&field_types)
        return false
    }

    layout := compute_natural_layout(
        semantic_package,
        array.view(&field_types),
    )
    if !layout.known {
        if !layout.overflow {
            for field_type in array.view(&field_types) {
                (dependency, found) := missing_layout_symbol(
                    semantic_package,
                    field_type,
                )
                if found {
                    blocked_symbol^ = dependency
                    break
                }
            }
        }
        array.destroy(&fields)
        array.destroy(&field_types)
        return false
    }

    next_offset: u64 = 0
    for index: usize = 0; index < fields.length; index += 1 {
        field_type := &semantic_package.types.data[
            cast[usize](fields.data[index].type.value)
        ]
        (offset, aligned) := aligned_offset(
            next_offset,
            field_type.byte_alignment,
        )
        assert(aligned && field_type.byte_size <= ~cast[u64](0) - offset,
            "completed natural layout changed during struct publication")
        fields.data[index].byte_offset = offset
        next_offset = offset + field_type.byte_size
    }

    member_begin := semantic_package.type_members.length
    nominal_member_begin := semantic_package.nominal_members.length
    for field_type in array.view(&field_types) {
        array.append(&semantic_package.type_members, field_type)
    }
    for field in array.view(&fields) {
        array.append(&semantic_package.nominal_members, field)
    }
    completed := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](struct_type.value)]
    completed.layout_known = true
    completed.byte_size = layout.size
    completed.byte_alignment = layout.alignment
    completed.member_begin = member_begin
    completed.member_count = field_types.length
    completed.nominal_member_begin = nominal_member_begin
    completed.nominal_member_count = fields.length
    array.destroy(&fields)
    array.destroy(&field_types)
    return true
}

init_semantic_package :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    id: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
) {
    semantic_package.workspace_package = id
    semantic_package.package_scope = invalid_scope_id()
    array.init(&semantic_package.scopes)
    array.init(&semantic_package.symbols)
    array.init(&semantic_package.files)
    array.init(&semantic_package.imports)
    array.init(&semantic_package.imported_names)
    init_semantic_types(semantic_package)
    array.init(&semantic_package.conditional_declarations)
    array.init(&semantic_package.conditional_selections)
    array.init(&semantic_package.compile_time_products)
    semantic_package.indexed_condition_count = 0
    semantic_package.indexed_compile_time_symbol_count = 0
    semantic_package.unconditional_symbol_count = 0
    array.init(&semantic_package.graph_import_edges)
    semantic_package.typed_interface_built = false
}

destroy_semantic_package :: proc(semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package) {
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.scopes.length;
        index += 1 {
        array.destroy(&semantic_package.scopes.data[index].symbols)
    }
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.graph_import_edges)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.interface_declarations)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.interface_type_translations)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.interface_nominal_members)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.interface_type_members)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.interface_types)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.imported_typed_names)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.imported_types)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.nominal_members)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.type_members)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.types)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.compile_time_products)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.conditional_selections)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.conditional_declarations)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.imported_names)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.imports)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.files)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.symbols)
    array.destroy(&semantic_package.scopes)
    semantic_package.workspace_package = compiler_workspace.Package_Id{}
    semantic_package.package_scope = invalid_scope_id()
    semantic_package.indexed_condition_count = 0
    semantic_package.indexed_compile_time_symbol_count = 0
    semantic_package.unconditional_symbol_count = 0
    semantic_package.typed_interface_built = false
}

// collect_workspace_declarations constructs every package row, indexes graph
// edges in one global pass, then collects packages in stable graph order. graph
// remains borrowed. A failed graph initializes an empty result and returns
// false without entering semantics, letting process drivers use one unconditional
// ownership path while preserving the graph's diagnostics as the sole failure.
pub collect_workspace_declarations :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
) -> bool {
    array.init(&semantic.packages)
    array.init(&semantic.diagnostics)
    semantic.failed = false
    semantic.target_declarations_materialized = false
    semantic.public_names_bound = false
    semantic.typed_interfaces_built = false
    if graph.failed {
        semantic.failed = true
        return false
    }

    for index: usize = 0; index < graph.packages.length; index += 1 {
        semantic_package: Semantic_Package
        init_semantic_package(
            &semantic_package,
            compiler_workspace.Package_Id{value = cast[u32](index)},
        )
        array.append(&semantic.packages, semantic_package)
        empty: Semantic_Package
        semantic_package = empty
    }

    for edge_index: usize = 0;
        edge_index < graph.imports.length;
        edge_index += 1 {
        edge := &graph.imports.data[edge_index]
        assert(compiler_workspace.package_id_valid(edge.importing_package) &&
            cast[usize](edge.importing_package.value) < semantic.packages.length,
            "workspace import consumer is outside semantic package table")
        semantic_package := &semantic.packages.data[
            cast[usize](edge.importing_package.value)
        ]
        array.append(&semantic_package.graph_import_edges, edge_index)
    }

    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic.packages.length; index += 1 {
        collector := Collector{
            graph = graph,
            semantic = semantic,
            semantic_package = &semantic.packages.data[index],
            workspace_package = &graph.packages.data[index],
        }
        collect_package(&collector)
    }
    return !semantic.failed
}

// Target_Facts is the LLVM-independent semantic projection required by the
// first self-hosted compile-time selector. Text fields use the specification's
// stable target spellings; pointer_bits and page_size are exact unsigned
// compile-time integers. The value owns no allocation because every string
// refers to a process-lifetime literal.
pub Target_Facts :: struct {
    identity: string,
    arch: string,
    os: string,
    abi: string,
    byte_order: string,
    object_format: string,
    file_tag: string,
    pointer_bits: u64,
    page_size: u64,
}

strings_equal :: proc(left, right: string) -> bool {
    if len(left) != len(right) {
        return false
    }
    for index: usize = 0; index < len(left); index += 1 {
        if left[index] != right[index] {
            return false
        }
    }
    return true
}

// select_builtin_target_facts maps the four public target selectors to the
// same versioned semantic facts as the bootstrap profiles. An unknown selector
// returns false and a zero value; CLI validation remains the caller's policy.
pub select_builtin_target_facts :: proc(
    selector: string,
) -> (Target_Facts, bool) {
    facts: Target_Facts
    facts.pointer_bits = 64
    facts.byte_order = "little"
    if strings_equal(selector, "aarch64-macos") {
        facts.identity = "draft-aarch64-macos-v6"
        facts.arch = "aarch64"
        facts.os = "macos"
        facts.abi = "darwin_arm64"
        facts.object_format = "macho"
        facts.file_tag = "aarch64-macos"
        facts.page_size = 16384
        return (facts, true)
    }
    if strings_equal(selector, "aarch64-linux") {
        facts.identity = "draft-aarch64-linux-gnu-v2"
        facts.arch = "aarch64"
        facts.os = "linux"
        facts.abi = "aapcs64_gnu"
        facts.object_format = "elf"
        facts.file_tag = "aarch64-linux"
        facts.page_size = 4096
        return (facts, true)
    }
    if strings_equal(selector, "x86_64-linux") {
        facts.identity = "draft-x86_64-linux-gnu-v2"
        facts.arch = "x86_64"
        facts.os = "linux"
        facts.abi = "sysv_amd64"
        facts.object_format = "elf"
        facts.file_tag = "x86_64-linux"
        facts.page_size = 4096
        return (facts, true)
    }
    if strings_equal(selector, "x86_64-windows") {
        facts.identity = "draft-x86_64-windows-msvc-v2"
        facts.arch = "x86_64"
        facts.os = "windows"
        facts.abi = "win64"
        facts.object_format = "coff"
        facts.file_tag = "x86_64-windows"
        facts.page_size = 4096
        return (facts, true)
    }
    empty: Target_Facts
    return (empty, false)
}

invalid_compile_time_value :: proc() -> Compile_Time_Value {
    value: Compile_Time_Value
    value.kind = .invalid
    value.static_type = invalid_type_id()
    value.type_value = invalid_type_id()
    return value
}

// append_compile_time_product assigns the next stable package-local product
// ID. Callers retain IDs rather than pointers because Dynamic growth may move
// the table. The all-ones sentinel is kept outside the valid index domain.
append_compile_time_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    product: Compile_Time_Product,
) -> Compile_Time_Product_Id {
    assert(semantic_package.compile_time_products.length <
        cast[usize](Invalid_Compile_Time_Product_Value),
        "compile-time product table exceeds u32 identity space")
    id := Compile_Time_Product_Id{
        value = cast[u32](semantic_package.compile_time_products.length),
    }
    array.append(&semantic_package.compile_time_products, product)
    return id
}

// find_constant_product returns the unique source-row product for symbol.
// Candidate rows are indexed before an evaluator may request one, so absence
// means that the name is not a constant supported by this staging boundary.
find_constant_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
) -> (Compile_Time_Product_Id, bool) {
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.kind == .constant &&
            product.symbol.value == symbol.value {
            return (Compile_Time_Product_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_compile_time_product_id(), false)
}

// find_declaration_product returns the stable type/classification producer for
// one package binding. Every visible package symbol receives exactly one row
// before either the condition or interface scheduler can demand it.
find_declaration_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
) -> (Compile_Time_Product_Id, bool) {
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.kind == .declaration &&
            product.symbol.value == symbol.value {
            return (Compile_Time_Product_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_compile_time_product_id(), false)
}

// index_visible_compile_time_products extends the package product table after
// initial collection and after each selected branch. Newly reachable condition
// sites precede newly visible declaration and constant rows, matching the
// production work graph's source-mutation frontier. Both later product kinds
// remain dormant until a condition or typed public interface demands them: the
// narrow staging evaluator must not reject an unrelated declaration merely
// because its aggregate, type, or procedural vocabulary has not moved yet.
index_visible_compile_time_products :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
) {
    for semantic_package.indexed_condition_count <
        semantic_package.conditional_declarations.length {
        product: Compile_Time_Product
        product.kind = .condition
        product.state = .waiting
        product.symbol = invalid_symbol_id()
        product.condition_index = semantic_package.indexed_condition_count
        product.dependency = invalid_compile_time_product_id()
        append_compile_time_product(semantic_package, product)
        semantic_package.indexed_condition_count += 1
    }

    for semantic_package.indexed_compile_time_symbol_count <
        semantic_package.symbols.length {
        symbol_index := semantic_package.indexed_compile_time_symbol_count
        semantic_package.indexed_compile_time_symbol_count += 1
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[symbol_index]
        if symbol.scope.value != semantic_package.package_scope.value {
            continue
        }
        symbol_id := Symbol_Id{value = cast[u32](symbol_index)}
        declaration_product: Compile_Time_Product
        declaration_product.kind = .declaration
        declaration_product.state = .dormant
        declaration_product.symbol = symbol_id
        declaration_product.dependency = invalid_compile_time_product_id()
        append_compile_time_product(semantic_package, declaration_product)

        if symbol.kind == .constant ||
            symbol.kind == .unresolved_declaration || symbol.kind == .type {
            constant_product: Compile_Time_Product
            constant_product.kind = .constant
            constant_product.state = .dormant
            constant_product.symbol = symbol_id
            constant_product.dependency = invalid_compile_time_product_id()
            append_compile_time_product(semantic_package, constant_product)
        }
    }
}

// completed_constant_value is the sole local named-constant read available to
// an evaluator attempt. It never evaluates recursively. A false result causes
// the caller to return the exact Symbol_Id as a graph prerequisite.
completed_constant_value :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
) -> (Compile_Time_Value, bool) {
    (product_id, found) := find_constant_product(semantic_package, symbol)
    if found {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
            cast[usize](product_id.value)
        ]
        if product.state == .complete {
            return (product.value, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_compile_time_value(), false)
}

// demand_constant_product changes exactly one dormant constant to waiting and
// returns its stable row. Already demanded or completed rows retain state. The
// false result identifies an unsupported declaration category, not a scheduler
// edge which may become ready later.
demand_constant_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
) -> (Compile_Time_Product_Id, bool) {
    (product_id, found) := find_constant_product(semantic_package, symbol)
    if !found {
        return (invalid_compile_time_product_id(), false)
    }
    product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        cast[usize](product_id.value)
    ]
    if product.state == .dormant {
        product.state = .waiting
    }
    return (product_id, true)
}

// demand_declaration_product activates one public declaration or local
// dependency. Publication is monotonic; an already completed/error row retains
// its terminal state and identity.
demand_declaration_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
) -> (Compile_Time_Product_Id, bool) {
    (product_id, found) := find_declaration_product(semantic_package, symbol)
    if !found {
        return (invalid_compile_time_product_id(), false)
    }
    product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        cast[usize](product_id.value)
    ]
    if product.state == .dormant {
        product.state = .waiting
    }
    return (product_id, true)
}

target_condition_text_equal :: proc(
    left, right: Compile_Time_Value,
) -> bool {
    if left.text_from_source {
        if right.text_from_source {
            return bytes_equal(left.source_text, right.source_text)
        }
        return bytes_equal_text(left.source_text, right.profile_text)
    }
    if right.text_from_source {
        return bytes_equal_text(right.source_text, left.profile_text)
    }
    return strings_equal(left.profile_text, right.profile_text)
}

target_condition_values_equal :: proc(
    left, right: Compile_Time_Value,
) -> bool {
    if left.kind != right.kind {
        return false
    }
    switch left.kind {
    case .boolean:
        return left.boolean == right.boolean
    case .unsigned_integer:
        return left.unsigned_integer == right.unsigned_integer
    case .string_value, .architecture, .operating_system, .abi, .byte_order,
        .object_format:
        return target_condition_text_equal(left, right)
    case:
        return false
    }
}

// target_alternative_known enforces the specification's distinct categorical
// enum vocabularies before equality is evaluated. Comparing target.os with
// `.aarch64`, for example, is a semantic error rather than a false condition.
target_alternative_known :: proc(
    kind: Compile_Time_Value_Kind,
    spelling: []u8,
) -> bool {
    switch kind {
    case .architecture:
        return bytes_equal_text(spelling, "aarch64") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "x86_64")
    case .operating_system:
        return bytes_equal_text(spelling, "macos") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "linux") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "windows")
    case .abi:
        return bytes_equal_text(spelling, "darwin_arm64") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "aapcs64_gnu") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "sysv_amd64") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "win64")
    case .byte_order:
        return bytes_equal_text(spelling, "little") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "big")
    case .object_format:
        return bytes_equal_text(spelling, "macho") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "elf") ||
            bytes_equal_text(spelling, "coff")
    case:
        return false
    }
}

node_source_bytes :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> []u8 {
    return source_bytes(
        graph,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        file_index,
        compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, id).range,
    )
}

target_member_name :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    member_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> ([]u8, bool) {
    member := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, member_id)
    if member.kind != .member_expression || member.child_count != 1 {
        empty: []u8
        return (empty, false)
    }
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, member_id)
    base := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[0])
    if base.kind != .name_expression ||
        !bytes_equal_text(
            node_source_bytes(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[0],
            ),
            "target",
        ) {
        empty: []u8
        return (empty, false)
    }
    if member.token_end == 0 {
        empty: []u8
        return (empty, false)
    }
    token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](member.token_end - 1)]
    if !token_is_contextual_name(token.kind) {
        empty: []u8
        return (empty, false)
    }
    return (
        source_bytes(
            graph,
            semantic_package.workspace_package,
            file_index,
            token.range,
        ),
        true,
    )
}

// lookup_imported_typed_name resolves one already-tokenized two-part qualified
// name. Returning the plain row by value copies no ownership: every text/type
// field remains a view or stable ID owned by the semantic workspace.
lookup_imported_typed_name :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    alias_name, member_name: []u8,
) -> (Imported_Typed_Name, bool) {
    file_scope := invalid_scope_id()
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.files.length; index += 1 {
        semantic_file := semantic_package.files.data[index]
        if semantic_file.file_index == file_index {
            file_scope = semantic_file.scope
            break
        }
    }
    if !scope_id_valid(file_scope) {
        empty: Imported_Typed_Name
        return (empty, false)
    }
    (alias_symbol, found_alias) := lookup_direct(
        graph,
        semantic_package,
        file_scope,
        alias_name,
    )
    if !found_alias {
        empty: Imported_Typed_Name
        return (empty, false)
    }
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.imported_typed_names.length;
        index += 1 {
        imported := semantic_package.imported_typed_names.data[index]
        if imported.import_symbol.value == alias_symbol.value &&
            bytes_equal(imported.name, member_name) {
            return (imported, true)
        }
    }
    empty: Imported_Typed_Name
    return (empty, false)
}

// imported_typed_constant resolves one exact two-part `alias.member` against
// the consumer rows already reconstructed from a dependency interface. A type
// declaration is projected as a local meta-type value; an ordinary constant is
// copied from its reconstructed row. During target selection these rows are
// still empty, so both remain an explicit later-phase boundary. No dependency
// syntax or producer Type_Id is consulted here.
imported_typed_constant :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    member_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> (Compile_Time_Value, bool) {
    member := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, member_id)
    if member.kind != .member_expression || member.child_count != 1 ||
        member.token_end == 0 {
        return (invalid_compile_time_value(), false)
    }
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, member_id)
    base := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[0])
    if base.kind != .name_expression {
        return (invalid_compile_time_value(), false)
    }
    alias_name := node_source_bytes(
        graph,
        semantic_package,
        file_index,
        tree,
        children[0],
    )
    final_token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](member.token_end - 1)]
    if !token_is_contextual_name(final_token.kind) {
        return (invalid_compile_time_value(), false)
    }
    member_name := source_bytes(
        graph,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        file_index,
        final_token.range,
    )

    (imported, found_imported) := lookup_imported_typed_name(
        graph,
        semantic_package,
        file_index,
        alias_name,
        member_name,
    )
    if found_imported {
        if imported.kind == .type {
            value: Compile_Time_Value
            value.kind = .type_value
            value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 53}
            value.type_value = imported.local_type
            return (value, true)
        }
        if imported.has_constant {
            return (imported.constant, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_compile_time_value(), false)
}

// target_field_value projects one recognized member spelling into its distinct
// semantic category. An unknown member leaves kind invalid so the enclosing
// condition fails at its source range without inventing a target fact.
target_field_value :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    name: []u8,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
) -> Compile_Time_Value {
    value: Compile_Time_Value
    value.static_type = invalid_type_id()
    value.type_value = invalid_type_id()
    if bytes_equal_text(name, "identity") {
        value.kind = .string_value
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 52}
        value.profile_text = facts.identity
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "arch") {
        value.kind = .architecture
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 57}
        value.profile_text = facts.arch
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "os") {
        value.kind = .operating_system
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 58}
        value.profile_text = facts.os
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "abi") {
        value.kind = .abi
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 59}
        value.profile_text = facts.abi
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "byte_order") {
        value.kind = .byte_order
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 60}
        value.profile_text = facts.byte_order
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "object_format") {
        value.kind = .object_format
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 61}
        value.profile_text = facts.object_format
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "file_tag") {
        value.kind = .string_value
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 52}
        value.profile_text = facts.file_tag
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "pointer_bits") {
        value.kind = .unsigned_integer
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 20}
        value.unsigned_integer = facts.pointer_bits
    } else if bytes_equal_text(name, "page_size") {
        value.kind = .unsigned_integer
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 22}
        value.unsigned_integer = facts.page_size
    }
    // Target selection observes exactly the builtin table, while later typed
    // array counts may ask for page_size after earlier declarations have
    // interned structural rows. Those appends do not disturb the canonical
    // builtin prefix or the fixed Type_Ids used above.
    assert(semantic_package.types.length >= 62,
        "target facts require the canonical builtin type prefix")
    return value
}

digit_value :: proc(byte: u8) -> (u64, bool) {
    if byte >= cast[u8]('0') && byte <= cast[u8]('9') {
        return (cast[u64](byte - cast[u8]('0')), true)
    }
    if byte >= cast[u8]('a') && byte <= cast[u8]('f') {
        return (cast[u64](byte - cast[u8]('a')) + 10, true)
    }
    if byte >= cast[u8]('A') && byte <= cast[u8]('F') {
        return (cast[u64](byte - cast[u8]('A')) + 10, true)
    }
    return (0, false)
}

// parse_target_unsigned accepts the lexer-validated integer spelling but still
// checks overflow because target facts have the concrete u64 domain.
parse_target_unsigned :: proc(bytes: []u8) -> (u64, bool) {
    if len(bytes) == 0 {
        return (0, false)
    }
    base: u64 = 10
    index: usize = 0
    if len(bytes) >= 2 && bytes[0] == cast[u8]('0') {
        if bytes[1] == cast[u8]('b') {
            base = 2
            index = 2
        } else if bytes[1] == cast[u8]('o') {
            base = 8
            index = 2
        } else if bytes[1] == cast[u8]('x') {
            base = 16
            index = 2
        }
    }
    value: u64 = 0
    saw_digit := false
    maximum := ~cast[u64](0)
    for index < len(bytes) {
        byte := bytes[index]
        index += 1
        if byte == cast[u8]('_') {
            continue
        }
        (digit, valid) := digit_value(byte)
        if !valid || digit >= base || value > (maximum - digit) / base {
            return (0, false)
        }
        value = value * base + digit
        saw_digit = true
    }
    return (value, saw_digit)
}

// simple_string_literal returns the interior bytes only when no escape decoding
// is required. Raw backtick contents are already exact; quoted escapes remain
// for the later general constant evaluator rather than being partially decoded
// by this phase.
simple_string_literal :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    node: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Node,
) -> ([]u8, bool) {
    if node.token_begin + 1 != node.token_end {
        empty: []u8
        return (empty, false)
    }
    token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin)]
    if token.kind != .string_literal && token.kind != .raw_string_literal {
        empty: []u8
        return (empty, false)
    }
    spelling := source_bytes(
        graph,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        file_index,
        token.range,
    )
    if len(spelling) < 2 {
        empty: []u8
        return (empty, false)
    }
    if token.kind == .string_literal {
        for index: usize = 1; index + 1 < len(spelling); index += 1 {
            if spelling[index] == cast[u8]('\\') {
                empty: []u8
                return (empty, false)
            }
        }
    }
    return (spelling[1:len(spelling) - 1], true)
}

// target_feature mirrors the selected architecture's complete stable feature
// vocabulary. The second result distinguishes a known disabled feature from an
// unknown spelling, which the specification requires the caller to diagnose.
target_feature :: proc(
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    feature: []u8,
) -> (bool, bool) {
    if strings_equal(facts.arch, "aarch64") {
        known := bytes_equal_text(feature, "aes") ||
            bytes_equal_text(feature, "crc") ||
            bytes_equal_text(feature, "dotprod") ||
            bytes_equal_text(feature, "fp16") ||
            bytes_equal_text(feature, "neon") ||
            bytes_equal_text(feature, "sha2")
        return (bytes_equal_text(feature, "neon"), known)
    }
    known := bytes_equal_text(feature, "avx") ||
        bytes_equal_text(feature, "avx2") ||
        bytes_equal_text(feature, "sse2")
    return (bytes_equal_text(feature, "sse2"), known)
}

// binary_operator finds the one infix token between the parser's two child
// ranges. The parser has already established expression shape; this operation
// deliberately recognizes only operators in the current scalar-constant
// subset.
binary_operator :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    left, right: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Node,
) -> (compiler_syntax.Token_Kind, bool) {
    for index := left.token_end; index < right.token_begin; index += 1 {
        kind := tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](index)].kind
        switch kind {
        case .equal_equal, .bang_equal, .less, .less_equal, .greater,
            .greater_equal, .logical_and, .logical_or:
            return (kind, true)
        case:
        }
    }
    return (.end_of_file, false)
}

// resolve_named_type_syntax maps the only type syntax admitted by this first
// typed-interface slice: one predeclared/local name or one exact import member.
// Local aliases normally consume completed constant products and report the
// first unpublished Symbol_Id through blocked_symbol. A nominal struct shell is
// the one exception: once its own constant attempt has installed symbol.type,
// recursive fields may name that identity before layout is complete. Qualified
// names consume the consumer-local reconstruction built from a dependency
// interface; producer Type_Ids never cross this boundary.
resolve_named_type_syntax :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    blocked_symbol: ^Symbol_Id,
) -> (Type_Id, bool) {
    node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, id)
    if node.kind != .named_type {
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    token_count := node.token_end - node.token_begin
    if token_count == 1 {
        token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin)]
        if !token_is_contextual_name(token.kind) {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        name := source_bytes(
            graph,
            semantic_package.workspace_package,
            file_index,
            token.range,
        )
        (builtin, found_builtin) := find_builtin_type(semantic_package, name)
        if found_builtin {
            return (builtin, true)
        }
        (symbol_id, found_symbol) := lookup_direct(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            semantic_package.package_scope,
            name,
        )
        if !found_symbol {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[cast[usize](symbol_id.value)]
        if symbol.kind != .type && symbol.kind != .unresolved_declaration &&
            symbol.kind != .constant {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        if type_id_valid(symbol.type) {
            provisional := &semantic_package.types.data[
                cast[usize](symbol.type.value)
            ]
            if provisional.kind == .struct_type {
                return (symbol.type, true)
            }
        }
        (value, complete) := completed_constant_value(
            semantic_package,
            symbol_id,
        )
        if complete && value.kind == .type_value {
            return (value.type_value, true)
        }
        if !symbol_id_valid(blocked_symbol^) {
            blocked_symbol^ = symbol_id
        }
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    if token_count != 3 {
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    first := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin)]
    separator := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin + 1)]
    last := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin + 2)]
    if !token_is_contextual_name(first.kind) || separator.kind != .dot ||
        !token_is_contextual_name(last.kind) {
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    alias_name := source_bytes(
        graph,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        file_index,
        first.range,
    )
    member_name := source_bytes(
        graph,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        file_index,
        last.range,
    )
    (imported, found_imported) := lookup_imported_typed_name(
        graph,
        semantic_package,
        file_index,
        alias_name,
        member_name,
    )
    if found_imported && imported.kind == .type {
        return (imported.local_type, true)
    }
    if found_imported && imported.has_constant &&
        imported.constant.kind == .type_value {
        return (imported.constant.type_value, true)
    }
    return (invalid_type_id(), false)
}

// evaluate_target_condition_expression checks one syntax expression against
// the closed scalar domain. expected supplies contextual enum type information
// to `.alternative` nodes. A name consumes only a completed local constant
// product; an unpublished candidate writes its Symbol_Id to blocked_symbol and
// returns invalid without evaluating that declaration recursively. All other
// invalid results mean that syntax or types fall outside this staging subset.
// Both logical operands are checked even though the computed value uses
// short-circuit truth rules: Draft evaluation skips the dead operand, but its
// source must still type-check and this boundary must not hide an unsupported
// or unpublished dependency behind `false &&` or `true ||`.
evaluate_target_condition_expression :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    blocked_symbol: ^Symbol_Id,
    expected: Compile_Time_Value_Kind = .invalid,
) -> Compile_Time_Value {
    node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, id)
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, id)
    switch node.kind {
    case .named_type, .pointer_type, .multi_pointer_type, .slice_type,
        .array_type, .tuple_type, .procedure_type:
        (resolved, found_type) := resolve_type_syntax(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            id,
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
        )
        if !found_type {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        value: Compile_Time_Value
        value.kind = .type_value
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 53}
        value.type_value = resolved
        return value
    case .tuple_expression:
        // Parenthesized comma syntax is expression-ambiguous at parse time.
        // It becomes a tuple type value exactly when every source-ordered child
        // evaluates to a type value; ordinary tuple constants remain outside
        // this scalar/structural interface evaluator.
        if len(children) < 2 {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        members: array.Dynamic[Type_Id]
        array.init(&members)
        for child_id in children {
            child := evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                child_id,
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
                .type_value,
            )
            if child.kind != .type_value {
                array.destroy(&members)
                return invalid_compile_time_value()
            }
            array.append(&members, child.type_value)
        }
        type_value := intern_tuple_type(
            semantic_package,
            array.view(&members),
        )
        array.destroy(&members)
        value: Compile_Time_Value
        value.kind = .type_value
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 53}
        value.type_value = type_value
        return value
    case .literal_expression:
        if node.token_begin + 1 != node.token_end {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin)]
        if token.kind == .keyword_true || token.kind == .keyword_false {
            value: Compile_Time_Value
            value.kind = .boolean
            value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 4}
            value.type_value = invalid_type_id()
            value.boolean = token.kind == .keyword_true
            return value
        }
        if token.kind == .integer_literal {
            (integer, valid) := parse_target_unsigned(
                source_bytes(
                    graph,
                    semantic_package.workspace_package,
                    file_index,
                    token.range,
                ),
            )
            if valid {
                value: Compile_Time_Value
                value.kind = .unsigned_integer
                value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 2}
                value.type_value = invalid_type_id()
                value.unsigned_integer = integer
                return value
            }
        }
        (text, valid_text) := simple_string_literal(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            node,
        )
        if valid_text {
            value: Compile_Time_Value
            value.kind = .string_value
            value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 52}
            value.type_value = invalid_type_id()
            value.source_text = text
            value.text_from_source = true
            return value
        }
        return invalid_compile_time_value()
    case .name_expression:
        name := node_source_bytes(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            id,
        )
        (builtin, found_builtin) := find_builtin_type(semantic_package, name)
        if found_builtin {
            value: Compile_Time_Value
            value.kind = .type_value
            value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 53}
            value.type_value = builtin
            return value
        }
        (symbol_id, found) := lookup_direct(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            semantic_package.package_scope,
            name,
        )
        if !found {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[cast[usize](symbol_id.value)]
        if symbol.kind != .constant && symbol.kind != .type &&
            symbol.kind != .unresolved_declaration {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        (value, complete) := completed_constant_value(
            semantic_package,
            symbol_id,
        )
        if complete {
            return value
        }
        if !symbol_id_valid(blocked_symbol^) {
            blocked_symbol^ = symbol_id
        }
        return invalid_compile_time_value()
    case .contextual_alternative_expression:
        if expected != .architecture && expected != .operating_system &&
            expected != .abi && expected != .byte_order &&
            expected != .object_format {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        if node.token_end < node.token_begin + 2 {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        token := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_end - 1)]
        spelling := source_bytes(
            graph,
            semantic_package.workspace_package,
            file_index,
            token.range,
        )
        if !target_alternative_known(expected, spelling) {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        value: Compile_Time_Value
        value.kind = expected
        value.type_value = invalid_type_id()
        switch expected {
        case .architecture: value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 57}
        case .operating_system: value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 58}
        case .abi: value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 59}
        case .byte_order: value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 60}
        case .object_format: value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 61}
        case: value.static_type = invalid_type_id()
        }
        value.source_text = spelling
        value.text_from_source = true
        return value
    case .member_expression:
        (member, is_target_member) := target_member_name(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            id,
        )
        if is_target_member {
            return target_field_value(semantic_package, member, facts)
        }
        (imported, found_imported) := imported_typed_constant(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            id,
        )
        if found_imported {
            return imported
        }
        return invalid_compile_time_value()
    case .group_expression:
        if len(children) == 1 {
            return evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[0],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
                expected,
            )
        }
        return invalid_compile_time_value()
    case .unary_expression:
        if len(children) != 1 ||
            tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin)].kind != .bang {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        operand := evaluate_target_condition_expression(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            children[0],
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
            .boolean,
        )
        if operand.kind != .boolean {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        operand.boolean = !operand.boolean
        return operand
    case .call_expression:
        if len(children) != 2 {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        (member, is_target_member) := target_member_name(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            children[0],
        )
        if !is_target_member || !bytes_equal_text(member, "has_feature") {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        argument := evaluate_target_condition_expression(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            children[1],
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
            .string_value,
        )
        if argument.kind != .string_value || !argument.text_from_source {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        (enabled, known) := target_feature(facts, argument.source_text)
        if !known {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        value: Compile_Time_Value
        value.kind = .boolean
        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 4}
        value.type_value = invalid_type_id()
        value.boolean = enabled
        return value
    case .binary_expression:
        if len(children) != 2 {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        left_node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[0])
        right_node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[1])
        (operator, have_operator) := binary_operator(
            tree,
            left_node,
            right_node,
        )
        if !have_operator {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        if operator == .logical_and || operator == .logical_or {
            left := evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[0],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
                .boolean,
            )
            if left.kind != .boolean {
                return invalid_compile_time_value()
            }
            right := evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[1],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
                .boolean,
            )
            if right.kind != .boolean {
                return invalid_compile_time_value()
            }
            result: Compile_Time_Value
            result.kind = .boolean
            result.static_type = Type_Id{value = 4}
            result.type_value = invalid_type_id()
            if operator == .logical_and {
                result.boolean = left.boolean && right.boolean
            } else {
                result.boolean = left.boolean || right.boolean
            }
            return result
        }

        left: Compile_Time_Value
        right: Compile_Time_Value
        if left_node.kind == .contextual_alternative_expression {
            right = evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[1],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
            )
            left = evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[0],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
                right.kind,
            )
        } else {
            left = evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[0],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
            )
            right = evaluate_target_condition_expression(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[1],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
                left.kind,
            )
        }
        if left.kind == .invalid || right.kind == .invalid ||
            left.kind != right.kind {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }

        result: Compile_Time_Value
        result.kind = .boolean
        result.static_type = Type_Id{value = 4}
        result.type_value = invalid_type_id()
        if (operator == .equal_equal || operator == .bang_equal) &&
            left.kind != .string_value {
            if left.kind == .type_value {
                result.boolean = left.type_value.value == right.type_value.value
                if operator == .bang_equal {
                    result.boolean = !result.boolean
                }
                return result
            }
            result.boolean = target_condition_values_equal(left, right)
            if operator == .bang_equal {
                result.boolean = !result.boolean
            }
            return result
        }
        if left.kind != .unsigned_integer {
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        switch operator {
        case .less:
            result.boolean = left.unsigned_integer < right.unsigned_integer
        case .less_equal:
            result.boolean = left.unsigned_integer <= right.unsigned_integer
        case .greater:
            result.boolean = left.unsigned_integer > right.unsigned_integer
        case .greater_equal:
            result.boolean = left.unsigned_integer >= right.unsigned_integer
        case:
            return invalid_compile_time_value()
        }
        return result
    case:
        return invalid_compile_time_value()
    }
}

// first_ready_compile_time_product preserves the source replay boundary used by
// this phase oracle. The earliest waiting condition may run when its current
// edge is complete; while it is blocked, only demanded constant rows may run to
// satisfy that edge. A later independent condition therefore cannot append its
// branch before an earlier source condition. The production semantic executor
// may evaluate independent products concurrently, but its migration oracle
// replays published selections through the source collector in this canonical
// order, which is also the stable Symbol_Id order owned by this staging view.
// Dormant unrelated constants and terminal rows are skipped.
first_ready_compile_time_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
) -> (Compile_Time_Product_Id, bool) {
    waiting_condition := invalid_compile_time_product_id()
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.state != .waiting || product.kind != .condition {
            continue
        }
        waiting_condition = Compile_Time_Product_Id{
            value = cast[u32](index),
        }
        if !compile_time_product_id_valid(product.dependency) ||
            semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
                cast[usize](product.dependency.value)
            ].state == .complete {
            return (waiting_condition, true)
        }
        break
    }

    // Do not cross an earlier blocked condition with another condition. Only
    // named-value work can make its current prerequisite complete.
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.state != .waiting || product.kind != .constant {
            continue
        }
        if !compile_time_product_id_valid(product.dependency) ||
            semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
                cast[usize](product.dependency.value)
            ].state == .complete {
            return (Compile_Time_Product_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_compile_time_product_id(), false)
}

compile_time_product_state_present :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    state: Compile_Time_Product_State,
) -> bool {
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        if semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index].state == state {
            return true
        }
    }
    return false
}

// block_compile_time_product attaches the exact constant prerequisite returned
// by an evaluator attempt. Indexing has already created every visible candidate
// in source order. A missing row means the name is outside the supported local
// scalar-constant boundary and is therefore a terminal expression failure.
block_compile_time_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    product_id: Compile_Time_Product_Id,
    symbol: Symbol_Id,
) -> bool {
    (dependency, found) := demand_constant_product(
        semantic_package,
        symbol,
    )
    if !found {
        return false
    }
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        cast[usize](product_id.value)
    ].dependency = dependency
    return true
}

// append_unsupported_condition_diagnostic reports the precise expression which
// this staging evaluator cannot complete. The language itself has broader
// constant evaluation; this diagnostic is an explicit self-hosting boundary,
// never a guessed false branch.
append_unsupported_condition_diagnostic :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
) {
    append_diagnostic(
        semantic,
        .error,
        .unsupported_target_condition,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        file_index,
        range,
        .package_scope,
    )
}

// append_unsupported_typed_interface_diagnostic marks a declaration demanded
// by public interface construction which exceeds the deliberately narrow
// scalar/structural/distinct slice. The message describes implementation
// coverage, not a language rejection.
append_unsupported_typed_interface_diagnostic :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
) {
    append_diagnostic(
        semantic,
        .error,
        .unsupported_typed_interface,
        semantic_package.workspace_package,
        file_index,
        range,
        .package_scope,
    )
}

// append_unsupported_compile_time_diagnostic preserves the semantic consumer
// which demanded a shared constant product. Target selection and typed
// publication use the same evaluator and graph row, but their staging failures
// identify different replacement boundaries.
append_unsupported_compile_time_diagnostic :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    range: compiler_source.Source_Range,
    use: Compile_Time_Use,
) {
    switch use {
    case .target_selection:
        append_unsupported_condition_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            range,
        )
    case .typed_interface:
        append_unsupported_typed_interface_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            range,
        )
    }
}

// run_named_constant_product evaluates exactly one declaration payload
// against already completed scalar constants and target facts. A named
// `distinct T` and ordinary `struct { ... }` are handled here, rather than by
// the structural type resolver, because their identity belongs to the
// declaration symbol and package. A struct installs its nominal shell before
// resolving fields so pointer recursion is direct; unavailable by-value layout
// attaches one graph edge. Only a complete attempt publishes the constant
// value. Grouped constants and the broader Draft constant vocabulary remain
// outside this staging slice and fail only when a consumer demands them.
run_named_constant_product :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    workspace_package: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Package,
    product_id: Compile_Time_Product_Id,
    use: Compile_Time_Use,
) {
    product_index := cast[usize](product_id.value)
    product := semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[product_index]
    assert(product.kind == .constant && product.state == .waiting,
        "constant product is not ready to run")
    assert(cast[usize](product.symbol.value) <
        semantic_package.symbols.length,
        "constant product symbol exceeds semantic table")
    symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[
        cast[usize](product.symbol.value)
    ]
    source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(
        &workspace_package.loaded,
        symbol.syntax.file_index,
    )
    tree := &source_row.tree
    declaration := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, symbol.syntax.node)
    (payload_id, has_payload) := declaration_payload(tree, symbol.syntax.node)
    valid_declaration := declaration.kind == .declaration && has_payload
    if valid_declaration {
        children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
            tree,
            symbol.syntax.node,
        )
        valid_declaration = len(children) != 0 &&
            pattern_name_count(tree, children[0]) == 1
    }
    if !valid_declaration {
        append_unsupported_compile_time_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            declaration.range,
            use,
        )
        semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
            product_index
        ].state = .error
        return
    }

    payload := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, payload_id)
    blocked_symbol := invalid_symbol_id()
    value := invalid_compile_time_value()
    if payload.kind == .struct_type {
        root_identity := memory.owned_string_bytes(
            &workspace_package.identity.root_identity,
        )
        root_relative_path := memory.owned_string_bytes(
            &workspace_package.identity.root_relative_path,
        )
        public_name := symbol_name_bytes(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            symbol,
        )
        struct_type := intern_struct_type_shell(
            semantic_package,
            root_identity,
            root_relative_path,
            public_name,
        )
        symbol.type = struct_type
        if complete_plain_struct_type(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            tree,
            payload_id,
            struct_type,
            facts,
            &blocked_symbol,
        ) {
            value.kind = .type_value
            value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 53}
            value.type_value = struct_type
        }
    } else if payload.kind == .distinct_type {
        payload_children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
            tree,
            payload_id,
        )
        if len(payload_children) == 1 {
            (underlying, resolved) := resolve_type_syntax(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                symbol.syntax.file_index,
                tree,
                payload_children[0],
                facts,
                &blocked_symbol,
            )
            if resolved {
                root_identity := memory.owned_string_bytes(
                    &workspace_package.identity.root_identity,
                )
                root_relative_path := memory.owned_string_bytes(
                    &workspace_package.identity.root_relative_path,
                )
                public_name := symbol_name_bytes(
                    graph,
                    semantic_package,
                    symbol,
                )
                distinct_type := intern_distinct_type(
                    semantic_package,
                    root_identity,
                    root_relative_path,
                    public_name,
                    underlying,
                )
                if type_id_valid(distinct_type) {
                    symbol.type = distinct_type
                    distinct_row := &semantic_package.types.data[
                        cast[usize](distinct_type.value)
                    ]
                    if distinct_row.layout_known {
                        value.kind = .type_value
                        value.static_type = Type_Id{value = 53}
                        value.type_value = distinct_type
                    } else {
                        (dependency, found) := missing_layout_symbol(
                            semantic_package,
                            underlying,
                        )
                        if found {
                            blocked_symbol = dependency
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    } else {
        value = evaluate_target_condition_expression(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            tree,
            payload_id,
            facts,
            &blocked_symbol,
        )
    }
    if value.kind == .invalid {
        if symbol_id_valid(blocked_symbol) &&
            block_compile_time_product(
                semantic_package,
                product_id,
                blocked_symbol,
            ) {
            return
        }
        append_unsupported_compile_time_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            payload.range,
            use,
        )
        semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
            product_index
        ].state = .error
        return
    }

    // Reacquire the row after evaluation instead of retaining a pointer across
    // helper calls. The current attempt does not append products, but this rule
    // keeps pointer stability explicit if indexing later moves to ready waves.
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[product_index].value = value
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        product_index
    ].dependency = invalid_compile_time_product_id()
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        product_index
    ].state = .complete
}

// run_package_condition_product evaluates and publishes one package `when`.
// A completed condition appends exactly its selected declaration list to the
// retained package scope. Newly visible symbols and nested `else when` sites are
// indexed by the coordinator before the next product executes, preserving the
// unconditional Symbol_Id prefix and the production continuation ordering.
run_package_condition_product :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    workspace_package: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Package,
    product_id: Compile_Time_Product_Id,
) {
    product_index := cast[usize](product_id.value)
    product := semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[product_index]
    assert(product.kind == .condition && product.state == .waiting,
        "condition product is not ready to run")
    assert(product.condition_index <
        semantic_package.conditional_declarations.length,
        "condition product exceeds declaration table")
    region := semantic_package.conditional_declarations.data[
        product.condition_index
    ]
    assert(!region.materialized,
        "conditional declaration was materialized twice")
    source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(
        &workspace_package.loaded,
        region.syntax.file_index,
    )
    tree := &source_row.tree
    when_node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, region.syntax.node)
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, region.syntax.node)
    if when_node.kind != .when_declaration || len(children) < 2 {
        append_unsupported_condition_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            region.syntax.file_index,
            when_node.range,
        )
        semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
            product_index
        ].state = .error
        return
    }

    condition_node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[0])
    blocked_symbol := invalid_symbol_id()
    value := evaluate_target_condition_expression(
        graph,
        semantic_package,
        region.syntax.file_index,
        tree,
        children[0],
        facts,
        &blocked_symbol,
        .boolean,
    )
    if value.kind != .boolean {
        if symbol_id_valid(blocked_symbol) &&
            block_compile_time_product(
                semantic_package,
                product_id,
                blocked_symbol,
            ) {
            return
        }
        append_unsupported_condition_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            region.syntax.file_index,
            condition_node.range,
        )
        semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
            product_index
        ].state = .error
        return
    }

    semantic_package.conditional_declarations.data[
        product.condition_index
    ].materialized = true
    array.append(
        &semantic_package.conditional_selections,
        Conditional_Selection{
            syntax = region.syntax,
            select_true = value.boolean,
        },
    )
    collector := Collector{
        graph = graph,
        semantic = semantic,
        semantic_package = semantic_package,
        workspace_package = workspace_package,
    }
    if value.boolean {
        collect_declaration_list(
            &collector,
            tree,
            region.syntax.file_index,
            children[1],
            region.scope,
            region.collection_context,
        )
    } else if len(children) >= 3 {
        alternative := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, children[2])
        if alternative.kind == .when_declaration {
            collect_item(
                &collector,
                tree,
                region.syntax.file_index,
                children[2],
                region.scope,
                region.collection_context,
            )
        } else {
            collect_declaration_list(
                &collector,
                tree,
                region.syntax.file_index,
                children[2],
                region.scope,
                region.collection_context,
            )
        }
    }
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        product_index
    ].dependency = invalid_compile_time_product_id()
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        product_index
    ].state = .complete
}

// diagnose_stalled_compile_time_products distinguishes a real dependency cycle
// from a product already in terminal error. Every active constant is reachable
// from some package condition, so the earliest waiting condition is the most
// useful surface range. Falling back to a constant initializer protects the
// invariant if a future caller explicitly demands a root constant.
diagnose_stalled_compile_time_products :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    workspace_package: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Package,
) {
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.state != .waiting || product.kind != .condition {
            continue
        }
        region := semantic_package.conditional_declarations.data[
            product.condition_index
        ]
        source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(
            &workspace_package.loaded,
            region.syntax.file_index,
        )
        children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
            &source_row.tree,
            region.syntax.node,
        )
        range := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(
            &source_row.tree,
            region.syntax.node,
        ).range
        if len(children) != 0 {
            range = compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(
                &source_row.tree,
                children[0],
            ).range
        }
        append_unsupported_condition_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            region.syntax.file_index,
            range,
        )
        product.state = .error
        return
    }

    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.state != .waiting || product.kind != .constant {
            continue
        }
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[
            cast[usize](product.symbol.value)
        ]
        source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(
            &workspace_package.loaded,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
        )
        declaration := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(
            &source_row.tree,
            symbol.syntax.node,
        )
        append_unsupported_condition_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            declaration.range,
        )
        product.state = .error
        return
    }
}

// materialize_workspace_target_declarations selects package `when` branches
// through explicit condition and local named-scalar-constant products. Initial
// sites and constant candidates are indexed in canonical source order. A named
// value may depend on earlier or later local scalar constants, target fields,
// known target.has_feature calls, literals, `!`, `&&`, `||`, categorical
// equality, and unsigned comparisons. Strings remain valid values and feature
// arguments, but Draft strings have no language equality operator.
//
// General arithmetic, aggregates, types, imported constants, and compile-time
// procedures remain later products. Unsupported syntax emits one source
// diagnostic and selects no branch. Cycles leave an explicit waiting graph and
// fail at the earliest surface condition rather than recursing through source.
pub materialize_workspace_target_declarations :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
) -> bool {
    if graph.failed || semantic.failed {
        return false
    }
    assert(!semantic.target_declarations_materialized,
        "workspace target declarations are already materialized")
    assert(!semantic.public_names_bound,
        "target declarations must precede public-name binding")

    for package_index: usize = 0;
        package_index < semantic.packages.length;
        package_index += 1 {
        semantic_package := &semantic.packages.data[package_index]
        workspace_package := &graph.packages.data[package_index]
        for {
            index_visible_compile_time_products(semantic_package)
            (ready, found_ready) := first_ready_compile_time_product(
                semantic_package,
            )
            if !found_ready {
                if !compile_time_product_state_present(
                    semantic_package,
                    .waiting,
                ) {
                    break
                }
                if !compile_time_product_state_present(
                    semantic_package,
                    .error,
                ) {
                    diagnose_stalled_compile_time_products(
                        semantic,
                        semantic_package,
                        workspace_package,
                    )
                }
                break
            }

            kind := semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
                cast[usize](ready.value)
            ].kind
            switch kind {
            case .condition:
                run_package_condition_product(
                    graph,
                    facts,
                    semantic,
                    semantic_package,
                    workspace_package,
                    ready,
                )
            case .constant:
                run_named_constant_product(
                    graph,
                    facts,
                    semantic,
                    semantic_package,
                    workspace_package,
                    ready,
                    .target_selection,
                )
            case .declaration:
                assert(false,
                    "target selection scheduled a dormant declaration product")
            }
        }
    }
    if semantic.failed {
        return false
    }
    semantic.target_declarations_materialized = true
    return true
}

// bind_workspace_public_names builds the first cross-package name view only
// after every package has its declaration table for the caller's current
// boundary. Each accepted import receives a contiguous span of references to
// the target package's direct public declarations. Without target
// materialization this is the deliberately earlier unconditional view; after
// materialization it includes the selected target branches. File-local import
// aliases are not package declarations, so this operation naturally enforces
// the specification's no-re-export rule.
//
// This operation performs no type or constant work and emits no new user
// diagnostic. The caller must not invoke it after declaration errors, and may
// invoke it exactly once for one Semantic_Workspace. Canonical graph/package
// order and target declaration order completely determine the result.
pub bind_workspace_public_names :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
) -> bool {
    if graph.failed || semantic.failed {
        return false
    }
    assert(!semantic.public_names_bound,
        "workspace public names are already bound")
    assert(semantic.packages.length == graph.packages.length,
        "semantic package table is not aligned with workspace graph")

    for consumer_index: usize = 0;
        consumer_index < semantic.packages.length;
        consumer_index += 1 {
        consumer := &semantic.packages.data[consumer_index]
        for binding_index: usize = 0;
            binding_index < consumer.imports.length;
            binding_index += 1 {
            binding := &consumer.imports.data[binding_index]
            assert(binding.graph_import_index < graph.imports.length,
                "semantic import edge exceeds workspace graph")
            edge := &graph.imports.data[binding.graph_import_index]
            assert(cast[usize](edge.importing_package.value) == consumer_index,
                "semantic import edge belongs to another consumer")
            assert(compiler_workspace.package_id_valid(edge.imported_package) &&
                cast[usize](edge.imported_package.value) <
                    semantic.packages.length,
                "semantic import target is outside package table")

            binding.imported_name_begin = consumer.imported_names.length
            target := &semantic.packages.data[
                cast[usize](edge.imported_package.value)
            ]
            target_scope := &target.scopes.data[
                cast[usize](target.package_scope.value)
            ]
            for target_index: usize = 0;
                target_index < target_scope.symbols.length;
                target_index += 1 {
                target_symbol_id := target_scope.symbols.data[target_index]
                target_symbol := &target.symbols.data[
                    cast[usize](target_symbol_id.value)
                ]
                if target_symbol.visibility != .public {
                    continue
                }
                array.append(&consumer.imported_names, Imported_Name{
                    import_symbol = binding.symbol,
                    declaration = Symbol_Reference{
                        package_id = edge.imported_package,
                        symbol = target_symbol_id,
                    },
                })
            }
            binding.imported_name_count =
                consumer.imported_names.length - binding.imported_name_begin
        }
    }
    semantic.public_names_bound = true
    return true
}

// declaration_type_syntax returns the first explicit type child in one source
// declaration. It deliberately does not use declaration_payload: a variable
// initializer is the final payload while the declared type appears earlier.
// Constructor validity remains the responsibility of resolve_type_syntax.
declaration_type_syntax :: proc(
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    declaration_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
) -> (compiler_syntax.Node_Id, bool) {
    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
        tree,
        declaration_id,
    ) {
        child := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id)
        if node_is_type_syntax(child.kind) {
            return (child_id, true)
        }
    }
    return (compiler_syntax.Node_Id{}, false)
}

// resolve_type_syntax constructs the closed structural vocabulary admitted by
// this typed-interface slice. It resolves children recursively, interns exact
// package-local identities, and reports the first unpublished local constant or
// type through blocked_symbol. Array counts reuse the shared scalar compile-time
// evaluator, so literals, named local/imported untyped-or-usize constants, and
// target usize facts follow one dependency mechanism. Declaration-owned
// distinct syntax is intentionally constructed by the constant product which
// has the defining symbol; seeing it recursively here is invalid just as in
// production. Enums, variants, unions, specialized struct forms, SIMD, C
// procedure types, and parametric forms fail at this seam.
resolve_type_syntax :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    blocked_symbol: ^Symbol_Id,
) -> (Type_Id, bool) {
    node := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, id)
    children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, id)
    if node.kind == .named_type {
        // The parser represents a parenthesized grouped type as named_type with
        // one child. Its tokens are not a qualified spelling, so unwrap it here
        // before the leaf resolver examines exact name tokens.
        if len(children) == 1 {
            return resolve_type_syntax(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                children[0],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
            )
        }
        return resolve_named_type_syntax(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            id,
            blocked_symbol,
        )
    }
    if node.kind == .pointer_type || node.kind == .multi_pointer_type ||
        node.kind == .slice_type {
        if len(children) != 1 {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        (element, resolved) := resolve_type_syntax(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            children[0],
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
        )
        if !resolved {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        kind: Semantic_Type_Kind = .pointer_type
        if node.kind == .multi_pointer_type {
            kind = .multi_pointer_type
        } else if node.kind == .slice_type {
            kind = .slice_type
        }
        return (intern_element_type(semantic_package, kind, element), true)
    }
    if node.kind == .array_type {
        if len(children) != 2 {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        count := evaluate_target_condition_expression(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            children[0],
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
            .unsigned_integer,
        )
        count_converts_to_usize := count.kind == .unsigned_integer &&
            (count.static_type.value == 2 || count.static_type.value == 22)
        if !count_converts_to_usize || count.unsigned_integer == 0 {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        (element, resolved) := resolve_type_syntax(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            children[1],
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
        )
        if !resolved {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        return (
            intern_array_type(
                semantic_package,
                element,
                count.unsigned_integer,
            ),
            true,
        )
    }
    if node.kind == .tuple_type {
        if len(children) < 2 {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        members: array.Dynamic[Type_Id]
        array.init(&members)
        for child_id in children {
            (member, resolved) := resolve_type_syntax(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                child_id,
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
            )
            if !resolved {
                array.destroy(&members)
                return (invalid_type_id(), false)
            }
            array.append(&members, member)
        }
        result := intern_tuple_type(semantic_package, array.view(&members))
        array.destroy(&members)
        return (result, true)
    }
    if node.kind == .procedure_type {
        first := &tree.tokens.data[cast[usize](node.token_begin)]
        if first.kind == .keyword_c {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        return resolve_procedure_signature(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            file_index,
            tree,
            id,
            facts,
            blocked_symbol,
        )
    }
    return (invalid_type_id(), false)
}

// resolve_procedure_signature constructs the structural procedure type from
// fixed parameters followed by one result. Every parameter must have exactly
// one supported type and at least one source name; grouped names repeat that
// type in source order. Defaults, bodies, and local declarations do not affect
// the published procedure identity. Static packs were classified parametric
// during collection and are rejected by the caller.
resolve_procedure_signature :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    file_index: usize,
    tree: ^compiler_syntax.Syntax_Tree,
    procedure_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    blocked_symbol: ^Symbol_Id,
) -> (Type_Id, bool) {
    procedure := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, procedure_id)
    if procedure.kind != .procedure && procedure.kind != .procedure_type {
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    members: array.Dynamic[Type_Id]
    array.init(&members)
    result_type := Type_Id{value = 1}
    valid := true

    for child_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(tree, procedure_id) {
        child := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, child_id)
        if child.kind == .parameter_list {
            for parameter_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
                tree,
                child_id,
            ) {
                parameter := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(
                    tree,
                    parameter_id,
                )
                if parameter.kind != .parameter {
                    valid = false
                    break
                }
                parameter_type_id: compiler_syntax.Node_Id
                have_parameter_type := false
                for part_id in compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
                    tree,
                    parameter_id,
                ) {
                    part := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, part_id)
                    if node_is_type_syntax(part.kind) {
                        parameter_type_id = part_id
                        have_parameter_type = true
                        break
                    }
                }
                name_count := pattern_name_count(tree, parameter_id)
                if !have_parameter_type || name_count == 0 {
                    valid = false
                    break
                }
                (parameter_type, resolved) := resolve_type_syntax(
                    graph,
                    semantic_package,
                    file_index,
                    tree,
                    parameter_type_id,
                    facts,
                    blocked_symbol,
                )
                if !resolved {
                    valid = false
                    break
                }
                for name_index: usize = 0;
                    name_index < name_count;
                    name_index += 1 {
                    array.append(&members, parameter_type)
                }
            }
        } else if child.kind == .result_clause {
            result_children := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_children(
                tree,
                child_id,
            )
            if len(result_children) != 1 {
                valid = false
                break
            }
            (resolved_result, resolved) := resolve_type_syntax(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                file_index,
                tree,
                result_children[0],
                facts,
                blocked_symbol,
            )
            if !resolved {
                valid = false
                break
            }
            result_type = resolved_result
        }
    }

    if !valid {
        array.destroy(&members)
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    array.append(&members, result_type)
    type_id := intern_procedure_type(semantic_package, array.view(&members))
    array.destroy(&members)
    return (type_id, true)
}

// complete_typed_declaration_product resolves one public declaration or one
// local type/value dependency. Constants reuse the same product and evaluator
// as target selection. Variables publish their explicit named type; procedures
// publish a canonical fixed signature. Unsupported syntax fails closed at the
// declaration range and never manufactures a fallback type.
complete_typed_declaration_product :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    workspace_package: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Package,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    product_id: Compile_Time_Product_Id,
) {
    product_index := cast[usize](product_id.value)
    product := semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[product_index]
    assert(product.kind == .declaration && product.state == .waiting,
        "typed declaration product is not ready")
    symbol_index := cast[usize](product.symbol.value)
    assert(symbol_index < semantic_package.symbols.length,
        "typed declaration symbol exceeds semantic table")
    symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[symbol_index]
    source_row := compiler_workspace.file_at(
        &workspace_package.loaded,
        symbol.syntax.file_index,
    )
    tree := &source_row.tree
    declaration := compiler_syntax.syntax_tree_node(tree, symbol.syntax.node)
    blocked_symbol := invalid_symbol_id()
    resolved_type := invalid_type_id()
    resolved := false
    declaration_value := invalid_compile_time_value()

    if symbol.flags.parametric || symbol.flags.is_foreign ||
        symbol.flags.exported {
        resolved = false
    } else if symbol.kind == .constant || symbol.kind == .type ||
        symbol.kind == .unresolved_declaration {
        (constant_product, found_constant) := demand_constant_product(
            semantic_package,
            product.symbol,
        )
        if found_constant {
            constant := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
                cast[usize](constant_product.value)
            ]
            if constant.state != .complete {
                semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
                    product_index
                ].dependency = constant_product
                return
            }
            declaration_value = constant.value
            if declaration_value.kind == .type_value {
                resolved_type = declaration_value.type_value
                resolved = type_id_valid(resolved_type)
                symbol.kind = .type
            } else {
                resolved_type = declaration_value.static_type
                resolved = type_id_valid(resolved_type)
                if resolved {
                    symbol.kind = .constant
                }
            }
        }
    } else if symbol.kind == .variable {
        (type_syntax, have_type) := declaration_type_syntax(
            tree,
            symbol.syntax.node,
        )
        if have_type {
            (resolved_type, resolved) = resolve_type_syntax(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                symbol.syntax.file_index,
                tree,
                type_syntax,
                facts,
                &blocked_symbol,
            )
        }
    } else if symbol.kind == .procedure {
        (payload, have_payload) := declaration_payload(
            tree,
            symbol.syntax.node,
        )
        if have_payload {
            (resolved_type, resolved) = resolve_procedure_signature(
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                symbol.syntax.file_index,
                tree,
                payload,
                facts,
                &blocked_symbol,
            )
        }
    }

    if !resolved && symbol_id_valid(blocked_symbol) &&
        block_compile_time_product(
            semantic_package,
            product_id,
            blocked_symbol,
        ) {
        return
    }
    if !resolved {
        append_unsupported_typed_interface_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            semantic_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            declaration.range,
        )
        semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
            product_index
        ].state = .error
        return
    }

    symbol.type = resolved_type
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        product_index
    ].value = declaration_value
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        product_index
    ].dependency = invalid_compile_time_product_id()
    semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
        product_index
    ].state = .complete
}

// first_ready_typed_product selects one demanded declaration or scalar value
// whose current prerequisite is complete. Product table order supplies the
// deterministic tie-break. Conditions are already terminal after target
// materialization and dormant unrelated private products remain untouched.
first_ready_typed_product :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
) -> (Compile_Time_Product_Id, bool) {
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.state != .waiting || product.kind == .condition {
            continue
        }
        if !compile_time_product_id_valid(product.dependency) ||
            semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
                cast[usize](product.dependency.value)
            ].state == .complete {
            return (Compile_Time_Product_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}, true)
        }
    }
    return (invalid_compile_time_product_id(), false)
}

// diagnose_typed_product_cycle reports the first source-ordered demanded row
// left waiting when no ready edge exists. The product graph contains one exact
// dependency per attempt, so this state is a real local value/type cycle rather
// than a scheduling accident.
diagnose_typed_product_cycle :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
) {
    for index: usize = 0;
        index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
        index += 1 {
        product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
        if product.state != .waiting || product.kind == .condition {
            continue
        }
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[
            cast[usize](product.symbol.value)
        ]
        append_diagnostic(
            semantic,
            .error,
            .cyclic_typed_interface,
            semantic_package.workspace_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
            symbol.name_range,
            .package_scope,
        )
        semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index].state = .error
        return
    }
}

// type_package_public_declarations demands exactly the selected public symbol
// set, then executes its local prerequisite graph. Private declarations remain
// dormant unless a public type/value names them. Procedure bodies are outside
// interface identity and are intentionally not traversed.
type_package_public_declarations :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    workspace_package: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Package,
) -> bool {
    index_visible_compile_time_products(semantic_package)
    package_scope := &semantic_package.scopes.data[
        cast[usize](semantic_package.package_scope.value)
    ]
    for index: usize = 0; index < package_scope.symbols.length; index += 1 {
        symbol_id := package_scope.symbols.data[index]
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[cast[usize](symbol_id.value)]
        if symbol.visibility == .public {
            (ignored, found) := demand_declaration_product(
                semantic_package,
                symbol_id,
            )
            assert(found && compile_time_product_id_valid(ignored),
                "public symbol has no declaration product")
        }
    }

    for !semantic.failed {
        (ready, found_ready) := first_ready_typed_product(semantic_package)
        if !found_ready {
            waiting := false
            for index: usize = 0;
                index < semantic_package.compile_time_products.length;
                index += 1 {
                product := &semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[index]
                if product.state == .waiting && product.kind != .condition {
                    waiting = true
                    break
                }
            }
            if waiting {
                diagnose_typed_product_cycle(semantic, semantic_package)
            }
            break
        }
        product := semantic_package.compile_time_products.data[
            cast[usize](ready.value)
        ]
        switch product.kind {
        case .constant:
            run_named_constant_product(
                graph,
                facts,
                semantic,
                semantic_package,
                workspace_package,
                ready,
                .typed_interface,
            )
        case .declaration:
            complete_typed_declaration_product(
                graph,
                semantic,
                semantic_package,
                workspace_package,
                facts,
                ready,
            )
        case .condition:
            assert(false, "typed scheduler selected a condition product")
        }
    }
    return !semantic.failed
}

// ensure_interface_translation_table maintains one parallel memo slot for each
// current package-local type. Type construction is complete before interface
// publication for this slice, but growing to the observed length here keeps
// the ownership invariant local and explicit.
ensure_interface_translation_table :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
) {
    for semantic_package.interface_type_translations.length <
        semantic_package.types.length {
        array.append(
            &semantic_package.interface_type_translations,
            invalid_interface_type_id(),
        )
    }
}

// translate_interface_type lazily copies one local type graph into the
// package-independent interface domain. It publishes the memoized placeholder
// before following children, then gathers structural and named members in
// temporary storage so both final spans remain contiguous even when recursion
// appends other rows first. Struct layout and offsets are copied as semantic
// target facts, never recomputed from producer-local IDs during publication.
translate_interface_type :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    local_type: Type_Id,
) -> Interface_Type_Id {
    assert(type_id_valid(local_type) &&
        cast[usize](local_type.value) < semantic_package.types.length,
        "interface translation received an invalid local type")
    ensure_interface_translation_table(semantic_package)
    translation_index := cast[usize](local_type.value)
    existing := semantic_package.interface_type_translations.data[
        translation_index
    ]
    if interface_type_id_valid(existing) {
        return existing
    }

    assert(semantic_package.interface_types.length <
        cast[usize](Invalid_Interface_Type_Value),
        "interface type table exceeds u32 identity space")
    interface_id := Interface_Type_Id{
        value = cast[u32](semantic_package.interface_types.length),
    }
    placeholder: Interface_Type
    placeholder.element = invalid_interface_type_id()
    array.append(&semantic_package.interface_types, placeholder)
    semantic_package.interface_type_translations.data[
        translation_index
    ] = interface_id

    local := semantic_package.types.data[translation_index]
    translated_element := invalid_interface_type_id()
    if type_id_valid(local.element) {
        translated_element = translate_interface_type(
            semantic_package,
            local.element,
        )
    }
    translated_members: array.Dynamic[Interface_Type_Id]
    array.init(&translated_members)
    for member_index: usize = 0;
        member_index < local.member_count;
        member_index += 1 {
        member := semantic_package.type_members.data[
            local.member_begin + member_index
        ]
        array.append(
            &translated_members,
            translate_interface_type(semantic_package, member),
        )
    }
    member_begin := semantic_package.interface_type_members.length
    for member in array.view(&translated_members) {
        array.append(&semantic_package.interface_type_members, member)
    }
    array.destroy(&translated_members)

    translated_nominal_members: array.Dynamic[Interface_Nominal_Member]
    array.init(&translated_nominal_members)
    for member_index: usize = 0;
        member_index < local.nominal_member_count;
        member_index += 1 {
        member := &semantic_package.nominal_members.data[
            local.nominal_member_begin + member_index
        ]
        array.append(
            &translated_nominal_members,
            Interface_Nominal_Member{
                name = member.name,
                kind = member.kind,
                type = translate_interface_type(
                    semantic_package,
                    member.type,
                ),
                byte_offset = member.byte_offset,
            },
        )
    }
    nominal_member_begin := semantic_package.interface_nominal_members.length
    for member in array.view(&translated_nominal_members) {
        array.append(&semantic_package.interface_nominal_members, member)
    }
    array.destroy(&translated_nominal_members)

    semantic_package.interface_types.data[cast[usize](interface_id.value)] =
        Interface_Type{
            kind = local.kind,
            name = local.name,
            nominal_root_identity = local.nominal_root_identity,
            nominal_root_relative_path = local.nominal_root_relative_path,
            nominal_public_name = local.nominal_public_name,
            layout_known = local.layout_known,
            byte_size = local.byte_size,
            byte_alignment = local.byte_alignment,
            bit_width = local.bit_width,
            element = translated_element,
            element_count = local.element_count,
            member_begin = member_begin,
            member_count = local.member_count,
            nominal_member_begin = nominal_member_begin,
            nominal_member_count = local.nominal_member_count,
        }
    return interface_id
}

// translate_interface_constant rewrites both type-bearing positions of one
// completed local value through the canonical interface graph. Scalar payloads
// and borrowed text are otherwise copied unchanged.
translate_interface_constant :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    value: Compile_Time_Value,
) -> Interface_Constant_Value {
    result: Interface_Constant_Value
    result.kind = value.kind
    result.boolean = value.boolean
    result.unsigned_integer = value.unsigned_integer
    result.profile_text = value.profile_text
    result.source_text = value.source_text
    result.text_from_source = value.text_from_source
    result.static_type = translate_interface_type(
        semantic_package,
        value.static_type,
    )
    result.type_value = invalid_interface_type_id()
    if value.kind == .type_value {
        result.type_value = translate_interface_type(
            semantic_package,
            value.type_value,
        )
    }
    return result
}

// build_package_interface publishes selected public declarations in their
// canonical package-scope order. Every declaration product is terminal before
// entry, so this pass only translates stable types and optional constants; it
// performs no syntax resolution and cannot create a new dependency.
build_package_interface :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
) {
    package_scope := &semantic_package.scopes.data[
        cast[usize](semantic_package.package_scope.value)
    ]
    for index: usize = 0; index < package_scope.symbols.length; index += 1 {
        symbol_id := package_scope.symbols.data[index]
        symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[cast[usize](symbol_id.value)]
        if symbol.visibility != .public {
            continue
        }
        assert(type_id_valid(symbol.type),
            "public symbol reached interface publication without a type")
        interface_declaration: Interface_Declaration
        interface_declaration.source_symbol = symbol_id
        interface_declaration.name = symbol_name_bytes(
            graph,
            semantic_package,
            symbol,
        )
        interface_declaration.kind = symbol.kind
        interface_declaration.flags = symbol.flags
        interface_declaration.type = translate_interface_type(
            semantic_package,
            symbol.type,
        )
        (constant, completed_constant) := completed_constant_value(
            semantic_package,
            symbol_id,
        )
        has_constant := completed_constant && symbol.kind != .type
        interface_declaration.has_constant = has_constant
        if has_constant {
            interface_declaration.constant = translate_interface_constant(
                semantic_package,
                constant,
            )
        }
        array.append(
            &semantic_package.interface_declarations,
            interface_declaration,
        )
    }
    semantic_package.typed_interface_built = true
}

// complete_imported_struct_type validates and reconstructs one ordinary struct
// packet after its consumer-local shell and import memo have been installed.
// Member interface IDs are imported in source order, natural layout is
// independently recomputed, and every published size/alignment/offset is
// checked before becoming consumer state. Reconstructing an already complete
// nominal through another dependency path verifies exact member identity rather
// than silently accepting inconsistent interface graphs.
complete_imported_struct_type :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    consumer: ^Semantic_Package,
    target_package: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    source_type: ^Interface_Type,
    local_type: Type_Id,
) -> bool {
    target := &semantic.packages.data[cast[usize](target_package.value)]
    if !source_type.layout_known || source_type.byte_alignment == 0 ||
        source_type.member_count == 0 ||
        source_type.member_count != source_type.nominal_member_count ||
        source_type.member_begin > target.interface_type_members.length ||
        source_type.member_count >
            target.interface_type_members.length - source_type.member_begin ||
        source_type.nominal_member_begin >
            target.interface_nominal_members.length ||
        source_type.nominal_member_count >
            target.interface_nominal_members.length -
                source_type.nominal_member_begin {
        return false
    }

    fields: array.Dynamic[Semantic_Nominal_Member]
    field_types: array.Dynamic[Type_Id]
    array.init(&fields)
    array.init(&field_types)
    valid := true
    for index: usize = 0; index < source_type.member_count; index += 1 {
        source_member_type := target.interface_type_members.data[
            source_type.member_begin + index
        ]
        source_member := &target.interface_nominal_members.data[
            source_type.nominal_member_begin + index
        ]
        if source_member.kind != .field ||
            source_member.type.value != source_member_type.value ||
            len(source_member.name) == 0 {
            valid = false
            break
        }
        for prior in array.view(&fields) {
            if bytes_equal(prior.name, source_member.name) {
                valid = false
                break
            }
        }
        if !valid {
            break
        }
        (member_type, imported) := import_interface_type(
            semantic,
            consumer,
            target_package,
            source_member_type,
        )
        if !imported {
            valid = false
            break
        }
        array.append(&field_types, member_type)
        array.append(&fields, Semantic_Nominal_Member{
            name = source_member.name,
            kind = .field,
            type = member_type,
        })
    }
    if !valid {
        array.destroy(&field_types)
        array.destroy(&fields)
        return false
    }

    layout := compute_natural_layout(consumer, array.view(&field_types))
    if !layout.known || layout.overflow ||
        layout.size != source_type.byte_size ||
        layout.alignment != source_type.byte_alignment {
        array.destroy(&field_types)
        array.destroy(&fields)
        return false
    }
    next_offset: u64 = 0
    for index: usize = 0; index < fields.length; index += 1 {
        member_type := &consumer.types.data[
            cast[usize](fields.data[index].type.value)
        ]
        (offset, aligned) := aligned_offset(
            next_offset,
            member_type.byte_alignment,
        )
        if !aligned || member_type.byte_size > ~cast[u64](0) - offset ||
            offset != target.interface_nominal_members.data[
                source_type.nominal_member_begin + index
            ].byte_offset {
            valid = false
            break
        }
        fields.data[index].byte_offset = offset
        next_offset = offset + member_type.byte_size
    }
    if !valid {
        array.destroy(&field_types)
        array.destroy(&fields)
        return false
    }

    local := &consumer.types.data[cast[usize](local_type.value)]
    if local.layout_known {
        valid = local.byte_size == layout.size &&
            local.byte_alignment == layout.alignment &&
            local.member_count == field_types.length &&
            local.nominal_member_count == fields.length
        if valid {
            for index: usize = 0; index < fields.length; index += 1 {
                existing_type := consumer.type_members.data[
                    local.member_begin + index
                ]
                existing := &consumer.nominal_members.data[
                    local.nominal_member_begin + index
                ]
                if existing_type.value != field_types.data[index].value ||
                    existing.type.value != fields.data[index].type.value ||
                    existing.kind != fields.data[index].kind ||
                    existing.byte_offset != fields.data[index].byte_offset ||
                    !bytes_equal(existing.name, fields.data[index].name) {
                    valid = false
                    break
                }
            }
        }
    } else {
        member_begin := consumer.type_members.length
        nominal_member_begin := consumer.nominal_members.length
        for field_type in array.view(&field_types) {
            array.append(&consumer.type_members, field_type)
        }
        for field in array.view(&fields) {
            array.append(&consumer.nominal_members, field)
        }
        local = &consumer.types.data[cast[usize](local_type.value)]
        local.layout_known = true
        local.byte_size = layout.size
        local.byte_alignment = layout.alignment
        local.member_begin = member_begin
        local.member_count = field_types.length
        local.nominal_member_begin = nominal_member_begin
        local.nominal_member_count = fields.length
    }
    array.destroy(&field_types)
    array.destroy(&fields)
    return valid
}

// import_interface_type reconstructs one dependency interface identity in the
// consumer's local Type_Id domain. Predeclared scalar rows reuse the consumer's
// canonical builtins by exact kind/name. Pointer-like and array rows recursively
// rebuild their element, while tuple/procedure rows recursively rebuild their
// ordered member span; every structural root then passes through the matching
// consumer interner. Distinct rows recursively rebuild their underlying type.
// Struct rows memoize a nominal shell before rebuilding and validating their
// named member packet. Both nominal families use the producer's three-part key,
// so direct and transitive import paths converge without rebaptizing the type
// in the consumer. Every successful mapping is memoized by dependency package
// plus interface ID; the early struct memo is retained only in a workspace that
// will fail if packet validation does not complete.
import_interface_type :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    consumer: ^Semantic_Package,
    target_package: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    interface_type: Interface_Type_Id,
) -> (Type_Id, bool) {
    for index: usize = 0; index < consumer.imported_types.length; index += 1 {
        imported := consumer.imported_types.data[index]
        if imported.target_package.value == target_package.value &&
            imported.interface_type.value == interface_type.value {
            return (imported.local_type, true)
        }
    }
    assert(cast[usize](target_package.value) < semantic.packages.length,
        "typed import target exceeds semantic package table")
    target := &semantic.packages.data[cast[usize](target_package.value)]
    if !interface_type_id_valid(interface_type) ||
        cast[usize](interface_type.value) >= target.interface_types.length {
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    source_type := target.interface_types.data[
        cast[usize](interface_type.value)
    ]
    local_type := invalid_type_id()

    if source_type.kind == .struct_type {
        complete_identity := len(source_type.nominal_root_identity) != 0 &&
            len(source_type.nominal_root_relative_path) != 0 &&
            len(source_type.nominal_public_name) != 0
        if !complete_identity {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        local_type = intern_struct_type_shell(
            consumer,
            source_type.nominal_root_identity,
            source_type.nominal_root_relative_path,
            source_type.nominal_public_name,
        )
        array.append(&consumer.imported_types, Imported_Type{
            target_package = target_package,
            interface_type = interface_type,
            local_type = local_type,
        })
        if !complete_imported_struct_type(
            semantic,
            consumer,
            target_package,
            &source_type,
            local_type,
        ) {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        return (local_type, true)
    } else if source_type.kind == .pointer_type ||
        source_type.kind == .multi_pointer_type ||
        source_type.kind == .slice_type {
        if !interface_type_id_valid(source_type.element) {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        (local_element, imported) := import_interface_type(
            semantic,
            consumer,
            target_package,
            source_type.element,
        )
        if imported {
            local_type = intern_element_type(
                consumer,
                source_type.kind,
                local_element,
            )
        }
    } else if source_type.kind == .array_type {
        if !interface_type_id_valid(source_type.element) ||
            source_type.element_count == 0 {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        (local_element, imported) := import_interface_type(
            semantic,
            consumer,
            target_package,
            source_type.element,
        )
        if imported {
            local_type = intern_array_type(
                consumer,
                local_element,
                source_type.element_count,
            )
        }
    } else if source_type.kind == .tuple_type ||
        source_type.kind == .procedure_type {
        if (source_type.kind == .tuple_type && source_type.member_count < 2) ||
            (source_type.kind == .procedure_type &&
                source_type.member_count == 0) {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        members: array.Dynamic[Type_Id]
        array.init(&members)
        valid := true
        for member_index: usize = 0;
            member_index < source_type.member_count;
            member_index += 1 {
            source_member := target.interface_type_members.data[
                source_type.member_begin + member_index
            ]
            (local_member, imported) := import_interface_type(
                semantic,
                consumer,
                target_package,
                source_member,
            )
            if !imported {
                valid = false
                break
            }
            array.append(&members, local_member)
        }
        if valid {
            if source_type.kind == .tuple_type {
                local_type = intern_tuple_type(consumer, array.view(&members))
            } else {
                local_type = intern_procedure_type(
                    consumer,
                    array.view(&members),
                )
            }
        }
        array.destroy(&members)
    } else if source_type.kind == .distinct_named_type {
        complete_identity := len(source_type.nominal_root_identity) != 0 &&
            len(source_type.nominal_root_relative_path) != 0 &&
            len(source_type.nominal_public_name) != 0
        if !complete_identity ||
            !interface_type_id_valid(source_type.element) {
            return (invalid_type_id(), false)
        }
        (local_underlying, imported) := import_interface_type(
            semantic,
            consumer,
            target_package,
            source_type.element,
        )
        if imported {
            local_type = intern_distinct_type(
                consumer,
                source_type.nominal_root_identity,
                source_type.nominal_root_relative_path,
                source_type.nominal_public_name,
                local_underlying,
            )
        }
    } else {
        for index: usize = 0; index < consumer.types.length; index += 1 {
            candidate := &consumer.types.data[index]
            if candidate.kind == source_type.kind &&
                strings_equal(candidate.name, source_type.name) {
                local_type = Type_Id{value = cast[u32](index)}
                break
            }
        }
    }
    if !type_id_valid(local_type) {
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    local_row := &consumer.types.data[cast[usize](local_type.value)]
    if local_row.layout_known != source_type.layout_known ||
        local_row.byte_size != source_type.byte_size ||
        local_row.byte_alignment != source_type.byte_alignment {
        return (invalid_type_id(), false)
    }
    array.append(&consumer.imported_types, Imported_Type{
        target_package = target_package,
        interface_type = interface_type,
        local_type = local_type,
    })
    return (local_type, true)
}

// import_interface_constant is the inverse of interface publication for one
// consumer. Both interface type IDs are reconstructed locally before the value
// is exposed beneath an import alias.
import_interface_constant :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    consumer: ^Semantic_Package,
    target_package: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    value: Interface_Constant_Value,
) -> (Compile_Time_Value, bool) {
    result: Compile_Time_Value
    result.kind = value.kind
    result.boolean = value.boolean
    result.unsigned_integer = value.unsigned_integer
    result.profile_text = value.profile_text
    result.source_text = value.source_text
    result.text_from_source = value.text_from_source
    (static_type, valid_static_type) := import_interface_type(
        semantic,
        consumer,
        target_package,
        value.static_type,
    )
    if !valid_static_type {
        return (invalid_compile_time_value(), false)
    }
    result.static_type = static_type
    result.type_value = invalid_type_id()
    if value.kind == .type_value {
        (type_value, valid_type_value) := import_interface_type(
            semantic,
            consumer,
            target_package,
            value.type_value,
        )
        if !valid_type_value {
            return (invalid_compile_time_value(), false)
        }
        result.type_value = type_value
    }
    return (result, true)
}

// bind_package_typed_imports replaces source-only public-name references with
// consumer-local type/value rows. Each import alias receives one contiguous
// span in producer public order. Failure is reported at the alias declaration;
// no partially reconstructed row is published after that point.
bind_package_typed_imports :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    consumer: ^Semantic_Package,
) -> bool {
    for binding_index: usize = 0;
        binding_index < consumer.imports.length;
        binding_index += 1 {
        binding := &consumer.imports.data[binding_index]
        edge := &graph.imports.data[binding.graph_import_index]
        target := &semantic.packages.data[
            cast[usize](edge.imported_package.value)
        ]
        assert(target.typed_interface_built,
            "typed import dependency has no published interface")
        binding.typed_name_begin = consumer.imported_typed_names.length
        for ordinal: usize = 0;
            ordinal < target.interface_declarations.length;
            ordinal += 1 {
            declaration := target.interface_declarations.data[ordinal]
            (local_type, imported_type) := import_interface_type(
                semantic,
                consumer,
                edge.imported_package,
                declaration.type,
            )
            if !imported_type {
                symbol := &consumer.symbols.data[
                    cast[usize](binding.symbol.value)
                ]
                append_unsupported_typed_interface_diagnostic(
                    semantic,
                    consumer,
                    symbol.syntax.file_index,
                    symbol.name_range,
                )
                return false
            }
            imported_name: Imported_Typed_Name
            imported_name.import_symbol = binding.symbol
            imported_name.declaration = Symbol_Reference{
                package_id = edge.imported_package,
                symbol = declaration.source_symbol,
            }
            imported_name.interface_ordinal = ordinal
            imported_name.name = declaration.name
            imported_name.kind = declaration.kind
            imported_name.local_type = local_type
            imported_name.has_constant = declaration.has_constant
            if declaration.has_constant {
                (constant, imported_constant) := import_interface_constant(
                    semantic,
                    consumer,
                    edge.imported_package,
                    declaration.constant,
                )
                if !imported_constant {
                    symbol := &consumer.symbols.data[
                        cast[usize](binding.symbol.value)
                    ]
                    append_unsupported_typed_interface_diagnostic(
                        semantic,
                        consumer,
                        symbol.syntax.file_index,
                        symbol.name_range,
                    )
                    return false
                }
                imported_name.constant = constant
            }
            array.append(&consumer.imported_typed_names, imported_name)
        }
        binding.typed_name_count =
            consumer.imported_typed_names.length - binding.typed_name_begin
    }
    return true
}

// package_typed_dependencies_ready checks only the source import occurrences
// owned by this consumer. Duplicate imports do not change readiness. The graph
// loader has already rejected package cycles, so a complete scan with no ready
// package is an internal invariant violation rather than user input recovery.
package_typed_dependencies_ready :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
) -> bool {
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic_package.imports.length; index += 1 {
        binding := &semantic_package.imports.data[index]
        edge := &graph.imports.data[binding.graph_import_index]
        if !semantic.packages.data[
            cast[usize](edge.imported_package.value)
        ].typed_interface_built {
            return false
        }
    }
    return true
}

// build_workspace_typed_interfaces is the first self-hosted typed package
// boundary. It visits packages dependency-first, reconstructs imported public
// types/values, executes demanded local declaration products, and publishes a
// canonical interface graph. The source graph and earlier public-name view
// remain borrowed and unchanged.
pub build_workspace_typed_interfaces :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
) -> bool {
    if graph.failed || semantic.failed {
        return false
    }
    assert(semantic.target_declarations_materialized,
        "typed interfaces require target declaration materialization")
    assert(semantic.public_names_bound,
        "typed interfaces require bound public names")
    assert(!semantic.typed_interfaces_built,
        "workspace typed interfaces are already built")

    built_count: usize = 0
    for built_count < semantic.packages.length && !semantic.failed {
        progressed := false
        for package_index: usize = 0;
            package_index < semantic.packages.length;
            package_index += 1 {
            semantic_package := &semantic.packages.data[package_index]
            if semantic_package.typed_interface_built ||
                !package_typed_dependencies_ready(
                    graph,
                    semantic,
                    semantic_package,
                ) {
                continue
            }
            if !bind_package_typed_imports(
                graph,
                semantic,
                semantic_package,
            ) {
                return false
            }
            if !type_package_public_declarations(
                graph,
                facts,
                semantic,
                semantic_package,
                &graph.packages.data[package_index],
            ) {
                return false
            }
            build_package_interface(graph, semantic_package)
            built_count += 1
            progressed = true
        }
        assert(progressed,
            "acyclic workspace has no ready typed-interface package")
    }
    if semantic.failed {
        return false
    }
    semantic.typed_interfaces_built = true
    return true
}

// lookup_import_member resolves one member beneath an already-resolved import
// alias. It searches only that binding's contiguous target-interface span and
// returns the target package/symbol identity, never a consumer-local copy.
// Absence is an ordinary lookup result; malformed IDs indicate a compiler
// invariant violation because callers obtain import symbols from lookup.
pub lookup_import_member :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    consumer_package: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    import_symbol: Symbol_Id,
    member_name: []u8,
) -> (Symbol_Reference, bool) {
    assert(semantic.public_names_bound,
        "import member lookup requires bound public names")
    assert(compiler_workspace.package_id_valid(consumer_package) &&
        cast[usize](consumer_package.value) < semantic.packages.length,
        "import member lookup package is invalid")
    consumer := &semantic.packages.data[
        cast[usize](consumer_package.value)
    ]
    assert(symbol_id_valid(import_symbol) &&
        cast[usize](import_symbol.value) < consumer.symbols.length,
        "import member lookup symbol is invalid")

    for binding_index: usize = 0;
        binding_index < consumer.imports.length;
        binding_index += 1 {
        binding := &consumer.imports.data[binding_index]
        if binding.symbol.value != import_symbol.value {
            continue
        }
        assert(binding.imported_name_begin <= consumer.imported_names.length &&
            binding.imported_name_count <=
                consumer.imported_names.length - binding.imported_name_begin,
            "imported name span exceeds consumer table")
        end := binding.imported_name_begin + binding.imported_name_count
        for index := binding.imported_name_begin; index < end; index += 1 {
            imported := consumer.imported_names.data[index]
            target := &semantic.packages.data[
                cast[usize](imported.declaration.package_id.value)
            ]
            target_symbol := &target.symbols.data[
                cast[usize](imported.declaration.symbol.value)
            ]
            if bytes_equal(
                symbol_name_bytes(graph, target, target_symbol),
                member_name,
            ) {
                return (imported.declaration, true)
            }
        }
        empty: Symbol_Reference
        return (empty, false)
    }
    empty: Symbol_Reference
    return (empty, false)
}

// lookup_qualified_name performs the exact two-stage lookup for
// `alias.member`: lexical lookup selects a file-local import alias, then the
// alias's bound public-name span selects a target declaration. A package
// declaration which shadows the requested alias is not treated as an import.
// Deeper aggregate/nominal selection belongs to typed member resolution.
pub lookup_qualified_name :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    consumer_package: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    lexical_scope: Scope_Id,
    alias_name, member_name: []u8,
) -> (Symbol_Reference, bool) {
    assert(compiler_workspace.package_id_valid(consumer_package) &&
        cast[usize](consumer_package.value) < semantic.packages.length,
        "qualified lookup package is invalid")
    consumer := &semantic.packages.data[
        cast[usize](consumer_package.value)
    ]
    (alias, found_alias) := lookup(
        graph,
        consumer,
        lexical_scope,
        alias_name,
    )
    if !found_alias || consumer.symbols.data[
        cast[usize](alias.value)
    ].kind != .import_alias {
        empty: Symbol_Reference
        return (empty, false)
    }
    return lookup_import_member(
        graph,
        semantic,
        consumer_package,
        alias,
        member_name,
    )
}

// destroy_semantic_workspace releases every table. The borrowed graph is not
// touched and may be destroyed only after this call if diagnostics or dumps are
// no longer needed.
pub destroy_semantic_workspace :: proc(semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace) {
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic.packages.length; index += 1 {
        destroy_semantic_package(&semantic.packages.data[index])
    }
    array.destroy(&semantic.diagnostics)
    array.destroy(&semantic.packages)
    semantic.failed = false
    semantic.target_declarations_materialized = false
    semantic.public_names_bound = false
    semantic.typed_interfaces_built = false
}

append_bool :: proc(output: ^compiler_text.Builder, value: bool) {
    compiler_text.append_byte(
        output,
        cast[u8]('1') if value else cast[u8]('0'),
    )
}

relative_file_name :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    package_id: compiler_workspace.Package_Id,
    file_index: usize,
) -> []u8 {
    loaded := &graph.packages.data[cast[usize](package_id.value)].loaded
    return memory.owned_string_bytes(
        &compiler_workspace.file_at(loaded, file_index).relative_name,
    )
}

// dump_symbol_row writes one source-level symbol in the common qualification
// schema. label distinguishes the initial declaration prefix from symbols
// appended by selected `when` branches; every remaining field is identical.
dump_symbol_row :: proc(
    label: string,
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    package_index, symbol_index: usize,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[symbol_index]
    compiler_text.append_text(output, label)
    compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, symbol_index)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, cast[usize](symbol.scope.value))
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_bytes(
        output,
        relative_file_name(
            graph,
            semantic_package.workspace_package,
            symbol.syntax.file_index,
        ),
    )
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_bytes(
        output,
        symbol_name_bytes(graph, semantic_package, symbol),
    )
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, symbol_kind_text(symbol.kind))
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, visibility_text(symbol.visibility))
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    append_bool(output, symbol.flags.is_thread_local)
    append_bool(output, symbol.flags.is_foreign)
    append_bool(output, symbol.flags.exported)
    append_bool(output, symbol.flags.parametric)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    if symbol.has_foreign_provider {
        compiler_text.append_bytes(
            output,
            source_bytes(
                graph,
                semantic_package.workspace_package,
                symbol.syntax.file_index,
                symbol.foreign_provider_range,
            ),
        )
    } else {
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('-'))
    }
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    if symbol.has_linker_name {
        compiler_text.append_bytes(
            output,
            source_bytes(
                graph,
                semantic_package.workspace_package,
                symbol.syntax.file_index,
                symbol.linker_name_range,
            ),
        )
    } else {
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('-'))
    }
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
}

// dump_workspace_declarations appends the stable migration view after the
// caller's workspace-graph dump. Scope IDs make file-local alias placement
// visible; import bindings name canonical target package IDs; native spellings
// remain exact source bytes.
pub dump_workspace_declarations :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    for package_index: usize = 0;
        package_index < semantic.packages.length;
        package_index += 1 {
        semantic_package := &semantic.packages.data[package_index]
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "semantic-package ")
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, semantic_package.scopes.length)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, semantic_package.symbols.length)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, semantic_package.imports.length)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))

        for file_index: usize = 0;
            file_index < semantic_package.files.length;
            file_index += 1 {
            semantic_file := semantic_package.files.data[file_index]
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "file-scope ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](semantic_file.scope.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_bytes(
                output,
                relative_file_name(
                    graph,
                    semantic_package.workspace_package,
                    semantic_file.file_index,
                ),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        }

        for symbol_index: usize = 0;
            symbol_index < semantic_package.symbols.length;
            symbol_index += 1 {
            dump_symbol_row(
                "symbol ",
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                package_index,
                symbol_index,
                output,
            )
        }

        for import_index: usize = 0;
            import_index < semantic_package.imports.length;
            import_index += 1 {
            binding := semantic_package.imports.data[import_index]
            edge := &graph.imports.data[binding.graph_import_index]
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "import-binding ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](binding.symbol.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_bytes(
                output,
                memory.owned_string_bytes(&edge.path),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](edge.imported_package.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        }
    }
}

// dump_workspace_target_declarations appends the selected target facts, every
// declaration-condition decision in materialization order, and only the symbol
// suffix appended by those decisions. The unconditional prefix count makes
// stable Symbol_Id preservation explicit instead of requiring a consumer to
// infer it from the preceding dump.
pub dump_workspace_target_declarations :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    facts: ^Target_Facts,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    assert(semantic.target_declarations_materialized,
        "target declaration dump requires materialized conditions")
    compiler_text.append_text(output, "target-profile ")
    compiler_text.append_text(output, facts.identity)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, facts.arch)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, facts.os)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, facts.abi)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, facts.byte_order)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, facts.object_format)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_text(output, facts.file_tag)
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, cast[usize](facts.pointer_bits))
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
    compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, cast[usize](facts.page_size))
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))

    for package_index: usize = 0;
        package_index < semantic.packages.length;
        package_index += 1 {
        semantic_package := &semantic.packages.data[package_index]
        for selection_index: usize = 0;
            selection_index < semantic_package.conditional_selections.length;
            selection_index += 1 {
            selection := semantic_package.conditional_selections.data[
                selection_index
            ]
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "condition ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_bytes(
                output,
                relative_file_name(
                    graph,
                    semantic_package.workspace_package,
                    selection.syntax.file_index,
                ),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](selection.syntax.node.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            append_bool(output, selection.select_true)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        }

        assert(semantic_package.unconditional_symbol_count <=
            semantic_package.symbols.length,
            "unconditional symbol prefix exceeds selected declarations")
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "selected-symbol-set ")
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            semantic_package.unconditional_symbol_count,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            semantic_package.symbols.length -
                semantic_package.unconditional_symbol_count,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        for symbol_index := semantic_package.unconditional_symbol_count;
            symbol_index < semantic_package.symbols.length;
            symbol_index += 1 {
            dump_symbol_row(
                "selected-symbol ",
                graph,
                semantic_package,
                package_index,
                symbol_index,
                output,
            )
        }
    }
}

// dump_workspace_public_names appends the stable cross-package name view after
// the declaration dump. Public rows retain their defining Symbol_Id; imported
// rows retain the local alias, canonical target package, and exact defining
// Symbol_Id. Before writing each imported row the function repeats the public
// lookup operation and asserts identity equality, so the migration output also
// qualifies the lookup path rather than only the stored table layout.
pub dump_workspace_public_names :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    assert(semantic.public_names_bound,
        "public name dump requires bound workspace names")
    for package_index: usize = 0;
        package_index < semantic.packages.length;
        package_index += 1 {
        semantic_package := &semantic.packages.data[package_index]
        package_scope := &semantic_package.scopes.data[
            cast[usize](semantic_package.package_scope.value)
        ]
        public_count: usize = 0
        for symbol_index: usize = 0;
            symbol_index < package_scope.symbols.length;
            symbol_index += 1 {
            symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[
                cast[usize](package_scope.symbols.data[symbol_index].value)
            ]
            if symbol.visibility == .public {
                public_count += 1
            }
        }

        compiler_text.append_text(output, "public-name-set ")
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, public_count)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        for symbol_index: usize = 0;
            symbol_index < package_scope.symbols.length;
            symbol_index += 1 {
            symbol_id := package_scope.symbols.data[symbol_index]
            symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[
                cast[usize](symbol_id.value)
            ]
            if symbol.visibility != .public {
                continue
            }
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "public-name ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](symbol_id.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_bytes(
                output,
                symbol_name_bytes(graph, semantic_package, symbol),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        }

        for binding_index: usize = 0;
            binding_index < semantic_package.imports.length;
            binding_index += 1 {
            binding := &semantic_package.imports.data[binding_index]
            edge := &graph.imports.data[binding.graph_import_index]
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "imported-package ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](binding.symbol.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](edge.imported_package.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                binding.imported_name_count,
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))

            begin := binding.imported_name_begin
            end := begin + binding.imported_name_count
            for imported_index := begin;
                imported_index < end;
                imported_index += 1 {
                imported := semantic_package.imported_names.data[
                    imported_index
                ]
                target := &semantic.packages.data[
                    cast[usize](imported.declaration.package_id.value)
                ]
                target_symbol := &target.symbols.data[
                    cast[usize](imported.declaration.symbol.value)
                ]
                member_name := symbol_name_bytes(
                    graph,
                    target,
                    target_symbol,
                )
                alias_symbol := &semantic_package.symbols.data[
                    cast[usize](binding.symbol.value)
                ]
                (resolved, found) := lookup_qualified_name(
                    graph,
                    semantic,
                    semantic_package.workspace_package,
                    alias_symbol.scope,
                    symbol_name_bytes(
                        graph,
                        semantic_package,
                        alias_symbol,
                    ),
                    member_name,
                )
                assert(found &&
                    resolved.package_id.value ==
                        imported.declaration.package_id.value &&
                    resolved.symbol.value == imported.declaration.symbol.value,
                    "imported name dump disagrees with qualified lookup")

                compiler_text.append_text(output, "imported-name ")
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](binding.symbol.value),
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](imported.declaration.package_id.value),
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](imported.declaration.symbol.value),
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_bytes(output, member_name)
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
            }
        }
    }
}

// semantic_type_kind_text is the stable migration-dump spelling shared with
// the production TypeKind oracle. It is descriptive output, not persistent
// interface identity.
semantic_type_kind_text :: proc(kind: Semantic_Type_Kind) -> string {
    switch kind {
    case .invalid_type: return "invalid"
    case .void_type: return "void"
    case .untyped_integer_type: return "untyped-integer"
    case .untyped_float_type: return "untyped-float"
    case .boolean_type: return "bool"
    case .boolean_storage_type: return "boolean-storage"
    case .signed_integer_type: return "signed-integer"
    case .unsigned_integer_type: return "unsigned-integer"
    case .float_type: return "float"
    case .rune_type: return "rune"
    case .endian_scalar_type: return "endian-scalar"
    case .raw_pointer_type: return "raw-pointer"
    case .c_string_type: return "c-string"
    case .string_type: return "string"
    case .pointer_type: return "pointer"
    case .multi_pointer_type: return "multi-pointer"
    case .slice_type: return "slice"
    case .array_type: return "array"
    case .tuple_type: return "tuple"
    case .procedure_type: return "procedure"
    case .simd_vector_type: return "simd"
    case .struct_type: return "struct"
    case .enumeration_type: return "enum"
    case .variant_type: return "variant"
    case .union_type: return "union"
    case .distinct_named_type: return "distinct"
    case .type_parameter_type: return "type-parameter"
    case .meta_type_value: return "meta-type"
    }
}

append_type_name :: proc(output: ^compiler_text.Builder, name: string) {
    if len(name) == 0 {
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('-'))
    } else {
        compiler_text.append_text(output, name)
    }
}

// append_type_name_bytes is the borrowed-byte counterpart used by nominal
// identity fields. Empty is rendered as the same explicit '-' sentinel as an
// empty process string so every interface row retains a fixed field count.
append_type_name_bytes :: proc(
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
    name: []u8,
) {
    if len(name) == 0 {
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('-'))
    } else {
        compiler_text.append_bytes(output, name)
    }
}

// append_local_type_shape renders a consumer-local type without exposing its
// process-local Type_Id. Structural children are expanded using canonical Draft
// syntax, struct rows terminate at their package-qualified nominal identity,
// distinct rows include that identity plus their underlying shape, and named
// scalar leaves include kind and spelling. Struct termination is essential for
// recursive graphs and leaves the field packet to the interface-type rows. This
// is what makes imported reconstruction comparable even when production has
// interned unrelated private types earlier.
append_local_type_shape :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    type_id: Type_Id,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    assert(type_id_valid(type_id) &&
        cast[usize](type_id.value) < semantic_package.types.length,
        "typed import dump received an invalid local type")
    semantic_type := &semantic_package.types.data[cast[usize](type_id.value)]
    if semantic_type.kind == .pointer_type ||
        semantic_type.kind == .multi_pointer_type ||
        semantic_type.kind == .slice_type {
        if semantic_type.kind == .pointer_type {
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('^'))
        } else if semantic_type.kind == .multi_pointer_type {
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "[^]")
        } else {
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "[]")
        }
        append_local_type_shape(semantic_package, semantic_type.element, output)
        return
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .array_type {
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('['))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            cast[usize](semantic_type.element_count),
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](']'))
        append_local_type_shape(semantic_package, semantic_type.element, output)
        return
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .tuple_type {
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('('))
        for index: usize = 0;
            index < semantic_type.member_count;
            index += 1 {
            if index != 0 {
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](','))
            }
            append_local_type_shape(
                semantic_package,
                semantic_package.type_members.data[
                    semantic_type.member_begin + index
                ],
                output,
            )
        }
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](')'))
        return
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .procedure_type {
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "procedure(")
        parameter_count := semantic_type.member_count - 1
        for index: usize = 0; index < parameter_count; index += 1 {
            if index != 0 {
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](','))
            }
            append_local_type_shape(
                semantic_package,
                semantic_package.type_members.data[
                    semantic_type.member_begin + index
                ],
                output,
            )
        }
        compiler_text.append_text(output, ")->")
        append_local_type_shape(
            semantic_package,
            semantic_package.type_members.data[
                semantic_type.member_begin + parameter_count
            ],
            output,
        )
        return
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .distinct_named_type {
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "distinct:")
        compiler_text.append_bytes(
            output,
            semantic_type.nominal_root_identity,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](':'))
        compiler_text.append_bytes(
            output,
            semantic_type.nominal_root_relative_path,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('.'))
        compiler_text.append_bytes(output, semantic_type.nominal_public_name)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('('))
        append_local_type_shape(
            semantic_package,
            semantic_type.element,
            output,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](')'))
        return
    }
    if semantic_type.kind == .struct_type {
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "struct:")
        compiler_text.append_bytes(
            output,
            semantic_type.nominal_root_identity,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](':'))
        compiler_text.append_bytes(
            output,
            semantic_type.nominal_root_relative_path,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('.'))
        compiler_text.append_bytes(output, semantic_type.nominal_public_name)
        return
    }
    compiler_text.append_text(
        output,
        semantic_type_kind_text(semantic_type.kind),
    )
    compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](':'))
    append_type_name(output, semantic_type.name)
}

append_interface_constant :: proc(
    value: ^Interface_Constant_Value,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    switch value.kind {
    case .boolean:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "bool ")
        append_bool(output, value.boolean)
    case .unsigned_integer:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "integer ")
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            cast[usize](value.unsigned_integer),
        )
    case .string_value:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "string ")
        text_length := len(value.source_text) if value.text_from_source else
            len(value.profile_text)
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, text_length)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        if value.text_from_source {
            compiler_text.append_bytes(output, value.source_text)
        } else {
            compiler_text.append_text(output, value.profile_text)
        }
    case .type_value:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "type ")
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            cast[usize](value.type_value.value),
        )
    case .architecture, .operating_system, .abi, .byte_order, .object_format:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "target-category ")
        if value.text_from_source {
            compiler_text.append_bytes(output, value.source_text)
        } else {
            compiler_text.append_text(output, value.profile_text)
        }
    case .invalid:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "invalid")
    }
}

append_local_constant :: proc(
    semantic_package: ^Semantic_Package,
    value: ^Compile_Time_Value,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    switch value.kind {
    case .boolean:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "bool ")
        append_bool(output, value.boolean)
    case .unsigned_integer:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "integer ")
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            cast[usize](value.unsigned_integer),
        )
    case .string_value:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "string ")
        text_length := len(value.source_text) if value.text_from_source else
            len(value.profile_text)
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, text_length)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        if value.text_from_source {
            compiler_text.append_bytes(output, value.source_text)
        } else {
            compiler_text.append_text(output, value.profile_text)
        }
    case .type_value:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "type ")
        append_local_type_shape(semantic_package, value.type_value, output)
    case .architecture, .operating_system, .abi, .byte_order, .object_format:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "target-category ")
        if value.text_from_source {
            compiler_text.append_bytes(output, value.source_text)
        } else {
            compiler_text.append_text(output, value.profile_text)
        }
    case .invalid:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "invalid")
    }
}

// dump_workspace_interfaces appends the canonical producer interfaces and the
// consumer-local typed import view. Interface rows may expose their own IDs;
// imported rows use structural type shapes so unrelated local interning order
// cannot affect qualification output.
pub dump_workspace_interfaces :: proc(
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    assert(semantic.typed_interfaces_built,
        "typed interface dump requires a completed workspace phase")
    for package_index: usize = 0;
        package_index < semantic.packages.length;
        package_index += 1 {
        semantic_package := &semantic.packages.data[package_index]
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "interface-package ")
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            semantic_package.interface_types.length,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
        compiler_text.append_unsigned(
            output,
            semantic_package.interface_declarations.length,
        )
        compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))

        for type_index: usize = 0;
            type_index < semantic_package.interface_types.length;
            type_index += 1 {
            interface_type := &semantic_package.interface_types.data[
                type_index
            ]
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "interface-type ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, type_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_text(
                output,
                semantic_type_kind_text(interface_type.kind),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            if interface_type.kind == .distinct_named_type ||
                interface_type.kind == .struct_type {
                append_type_name_bytes(
                    output,
                    interface_type.nominal_public_name,
                )
            } else {
                append_type_name(output, interface_type.name)
            }
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            append_type_name_bytes(
                output,
                interface_type.nominal_root_identity,
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            append_type_name_bytes(
                output,
                interface_type.nominal_root_relative_path,
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            append_type_name_bytes(
                output,
                interface_type.nominal_public_name,
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            append_bool(output, interface_type.layout_known)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](interface_type.byte_size),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](interface_type.byte_alignment),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](interface_type.bit_width),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            if interface_type_id_valid(interface_type.element) {
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](interface_type.element.value),
                )
            } else {
                compiler_text.append_text(output, "invalid")
            }
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](interface_type.element_count),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, interface_type.member_count)
            for member_index: usize = 0;
                member_index < interface_type.member_count;
                member_index += 1 {
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](semantic_package.interface_type_members.data[
                        interface_type.member_begin + member_index
                    ].value),
                )
            }
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                interface_type.nominal_member_count,
            )
            for member_index: usize = 0;
                member_index < interface_type.nominal_member_count;
                member_index += 1 {
                member := &semantic_package.interface_nominal_members.data[
                    interface_type.nominal_member_begin + member_index
                ]
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_bytes(output, member.name)
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_text(
                    output,
                    symbol_kind_text(member.kind),
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](member.type.value),
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](member.byte_offset),
                )
            }
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        }

        for declaration_index: usize = 0;
            declaration_index < semantic_package.interface_declarations.length;
            declaration_index += 1 {
            declaration := &semantic_package.interface_declarations.data[
                declaration_index
            ]
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "interface-declaration ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, declaration_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_bytes(output, declaration.name)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_text(output, symbol_kind_text(declaration.kind))
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            append_bool(output, declaration.flags.is_thread_local)
            append_bool(output, declaration.flags.is_foreign)
            append_bool(output, declaration.flags.exported)
            append_bool(output, declaration.flags.parametric)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](declaration.type.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            if declaration.has_constant {
                append_interface_constant(&declaration.constant, output)
            } else {
                compiler_text.append_text(output, "none")
            }
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
        }

        for binding_index: usize = 0;
            binding_index < semantic_package.imports.length;
            binding_index += 1 {
            binding := &semantic_package.imports.data[binding_index]
            compiler_text.append_text(output, "typed-import ")
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                output,
                cast[usize](binding.symbol.value),
            )
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
            compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, binding.typed_name_count)
            compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))

            end := binding.typed_name_begin + binding.typed_name_count
            for imported_index := binding.typed_name_begin;
                imported_index < end;
                imported_index += 1 {
                imported := &semantic_package.imported_typed_names.data[
                    imported_index
                ]
                compiler_text.append_text(output, "typed-import-name ")
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, package_index)
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](binding.symbol.value),
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(
                    output,
                    cast[usize](imported.declaration.package_id.value),
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_unsigned(output, imported.interface_ordinal)
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                compiler_text.append_bytes(output, imported.name)
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                append_local_type_shape(
                    semantic_package,
                    imported.local_type,
                    output,
                )
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8](' '))
                if imported.has_constant {
                    append_local_constant(
                        semantic_package,
                        &imported.constant,
                        output,
                    )
                } else {
                    compiler_text.append_text(output, "none")
                }
                compiler_text.append_byte(output, cast[u8]('\n'))
            }
        }
    }
}

render_semantic_message :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    diagnostic: ^Semantic_Diagnostic,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    switch diagnostic.code {
    case .duplicate_declaration:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "duplicate declaration of '")
        compiler_text.append_bytes(
            output,
            source_bytes(
                graph,
                diagnostic.package_id,
                diagnostic.file_index,
                diagnostic.range,
            ),
        )
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "' in the same ")
        compiler_text.append_text(output, scope_kind_text(diagnostic.scope_kind))
        compiler_text.append_text(output, " scope")
    case .previous_declaration:
        compiler_text.append_text(output, "previous declaration is here")
    case .thread_local_non_variable:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "thread_local is valid only on a package variable declaration",
        )
    case .parametric_non_type_or_procedure:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "parametric parameters are valid only on type and procedure declarations",
        )
    case .linker_name_non_native:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "a linker symbol name is valid only on a foreign or exported procedure",
        )
    case .grouped_type:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "type declaration requires one binding name",
        )
    case .grouped_procedure:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "procedure declaration requires one binding name",
        )
    case .unsupported_target_condition:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "self-hosted package 'when' requires a supported scalar constant expression",
        )
    case .unsupported_typed_interface:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "self-hosted typed interface requires a supported scalar, structural, distinct, or ordinary struct declaration",
        )
    case .cyclic_typed_interface:
        compiler_text.append_text(
            output,
            "self-hosted typed interface contains a cyclic declaration dependency",
        )
    }
}

// render_workspace_diagnostics appends exact bootstrap-style source messages
// after graph diagnostics. Every message is assembled transiently from fixed
// text plus the borrowed declaration spelling.
pub render_workspace_diagnostics :: proc(
    graph: ^compiler_workspace.Workspace_Graph,
    semantic: ^Semantic_Workspace,
    output: ^compiler_text.Builder,
) {
    for index: usize = 0; index < semantic.diagnostics.length; index += 1 {
        diagnostic := &semantic.diagnostics.data[index]
        message: compiler_text.Builder
        compiler_text.init(&message)
        render_semantic_message(graph, diagnostic, &message)
        compiler_diagnostic.render_message_bytes(
            source_file(
                graph,
                diagnostic.package_id,
                diagnostic.file_index,
            ),
            diagnostic.severity,
            diagnostic.range,
            compiler_text.view(&message),
            output,
        )
        compiler_text.destroy(&message)
    }
}
